"version\":3,\"id\":\"01a1d143-208b-703c-a4ce-ad0f2f60ae0f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:39.819Z\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\omp-dock-chief-omp-IAixST\\\\work\"}\n{\"type\":\"model_change\",\"id\":\"5316e49f\",\"parentId\":null,\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.531Z\",\"model\":\"dock-gateway/dock-model\",\"resolvedModelIsFallback\":false}\n{\"type\":\"thinking_level_change\",\"id\":\"59044c83\",\"parentId\":\"5316e49f\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.531Z\",\"thinkingLevel\":null,\"configured\":null}\n{\"type\":\"custom\",\"customType\":\"chief-chat:state\",\"data\":{\"enabled\":true},\"id\":\"226b830b\",\"parentId\":\"59044c83\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.643Z\"}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"d41d7617\",\"parentId\":\"226b830b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.830Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perform the selected definition lookup once.\"}],\"attribution\":\"user\",\"timestamp\":1794512200784}}\n{\"type\":\"custom_message\",\"customType\":\"chief-chat:tools\",\"content\":\"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 需求分流\\r\\n\\r\\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\\r\\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\\r\\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 能力选择\\r\\n\\r\\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\\r\\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\\r\\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\\r\\n\\r\\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\\r\\n\\r\\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 批准与派发\\r\\n\\r\\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\\r\\n\\r\\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\\r\\n\\r\\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\\r\\n\\r\\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\\r\\n\\r\\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 工具契约\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\\r\\n\\r\\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\\r\\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\\r\\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\\r\\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\\r\\n\\r\\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\\r\\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\\r\\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\\r\\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\\r\\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\\r\\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\\r\\n\\r\\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 报告与结果\\r\\n\\r\\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\\r\\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\\r\\n- 实际执行对象；\\r\\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\\r\\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\\r\\n\\r\\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\\r\\n\\r\\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\\r\\n\\r\\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\\r\\n\\r\\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\\r\\n\\r\\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 角色边界\\r\\n\\r\\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\\r\\n\\r\\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\\r\\n\",\"display\":false,\"attribution\":\"agent\",\"id\":\"6b7ea515\",\"parentId\":\"d41d7617\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.792Z\"}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"eaf1631c\",\"parentId\":\"6b7ea515\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.854Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_dock_1\",\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"arguments\":{\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"},\"partialArgs\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\\\"}\",\"streamIndex\":0}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"dock-gateway\",\"model\":\"dock-model\",\"usage\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":0,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1794512200837,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-dock\",\"duration\":11.392700000000332,\"ttft\":10.529300000000148,\"completedAt\":1794512200854,\"contextSnapshot\":{\"promptTokens\":0,\"nonMessageTokens\":6968,\"compactionEpoch\":0}}}\n{\"type\":\"custom\",\"customType\":\"tool_execution_start\",\"data\":{\"toolCallId\":\"call_dock_1\",\"toolName\":\"chief_read_report\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.865Z\"},\"id\":\"8b631173\",\"parentId\":\"eaf1631c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.865Z\"}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"6cd8c959\",\"parentId\":\"8b631173\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.877Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_dock_1\",\"toolName\":\"chief_read_report\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"guidance\\\":\\\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\\\",\\\"process\\\":false,\\\"receipt\\\":null,\\\"received\\\":false,\\\"report\\\":{\\\"at\\\":1794512198510,\\\"body\\\":{\\\"background\\\":\\\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\\\",\\\"deliverables\\\":[\\\"C:/owned/draft.md\\\"],\\\"execution\\\":\\\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\\\",\\\"pendingDecisions\\\":[\\\"Does the draft meet requirements?\\\"],\\\"result\\\":\\\"blocked\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\\\"},\\\"delegationId\\\":\\\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\\\",\\\"from\\\":\\\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\\\"}}\"}],\"details\":{\"httpStatus\":200,\"body\":{\"guidance\":\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\",\"process\":false,\"receipt\":null,\"received\":false,\"report\":{\"at\":1794512198510,\"body\":{\"background\":\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\",\"deliverables\":[\"C:/owned/draft.md\"],\"execution\":\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\",\"pendingDecisions\":[\"Does the draft meet requirements?\"],\"result\":\"blocked\",\"summary\":\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\"},\"delegationId\":\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\",\"from\":\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\",\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}}},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1794512200876}}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"fd0957b3\",\"parentId\":\"6cd8c959\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:40.908Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Controlled protocol completion; not model-behavior evidence.\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"dock-gateway\",\"model\":\"dock-model\",\"usage\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":0,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1794512200904,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-dock\",\"duration\":3.0874000000003434,\"ttft\":2.528700000000299,\"completedAt\":1794512200908,\"contextSnapshot\":{\"promptTokens\":0,\"nonMessageTokens\":6968,\"compactionEpoch\":0}}}\n","requests":[{"index":1,"method":"POST","url":"http://127.0.0.1:1726/v1/chat/completions","file":"C:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\omp-dock-chief-omp-IAixST\\captures\\request-001-_v1_chat_completions.json","raw":"{\"model\":\"dock-model\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"RFC 2119 keywords: MUST, REQUIRED, SHOULD, RECOMMENDED, MAY, OPTIONAL. `NEVER` = `MUST NOT`; `AVOID` = `SHOULD NOT`.\\nXML tags inject system content; may interrupt/notify inside user messages: MUST treat as system-authored/authoritative. User content is sanitized.\\n\\n§ Role\\nYou are omp's trusted coding assistant.\\n\\n# Engineering\\n- Correctness, then six-month maintainability. Delete dead weight; prefer boring design to needless abstraction.\\n- Compiled code: NEVER avoidable allocation, copying, computation.\\n- Unexpected repo changes are the user's; adapt. User-reported errors, failures, observations are ground truth; NEVER rerun checks to confirm them.\\n- Final chat MAY use LaTeX math (`$`, `$$`) and color (`\\\\textcolor`, `\\\\colorbox`, `\\\\fcolorbox`).\\n- MAY emit ` ```mermaid ` blocks; terminal renders ASCII. Only genuine structure/flow, not trivia.\\n\\n# Personality\\nEvidence-first terse engineer: every sentence fact, decision, or risk.\\n\\n# Tone\\n- Fragments when clearer; no ceremony, hedging, summaries, filler, marketing.\\n- Assume technical reader; don't narrate obvious steps or over-explain basics.\\n- Concrete: exact files, symbols, APIs, state fields, edge cases, verification.\\n- Reasoning: facts, constraints, tradeoffs, decisions, checks. Conclusion first; evidence next.\\n- Uncertainty: state at claim; name tradeoff; choose boring/safe option.\\n- Code: invariants, risks, verification.\\n\\n# Reasoning Format\\nProblem: what's wrong. Decision: action & why. Check: breakage & verification. Next: concrete action.\\n\\n# Succinct Patterns\\n- Y → need update X. This is safe: Z. Could do A, but B avoids C.\\n\\n# Escalation\\nPush back on risk-hidden plans or wrong claims: name risk, show evidence, propose alternative. If overruled, execute user's call; don't relitigate.\\n\\n§ Runtime\\n# Internal URLs\\nMost FS/bash tools resolve these; path selectors: `read` docs.\\n- `agent://<id>`: output (status + progress while unpublished); nested IDs dotted, `/key/index` JSON path; write = message, `agent://all` broadcast only.\\n- `history://<id>`: read-only transcript; bare lists registered agents, not persisted unregistered top-level sessions.\\n- `artifact://<id>`: spilled output; page :N-M or :raw:N-M.\\n- `local://<name>.md`: shared artifact.\\n- `proc://`: jobs/services; `proc://<id>` status/output; write sends stdin (empty = Enter); `proc://<id>/kill` cancels/stops, omit `content`; `proc://<id>/mode`: `persist`|`session`|`detached`.\\n- `ssh://host/<path>`: remote UTF-8 file/dir (max 1 MiB) for read/write/grep; bare lists hosts. Encode `:` `?` `#` as %3A %3F %23. Needs verified POSIX shell; else bash remote SSH or sshfs.\\n- `mcp://<uri>`: MCP resource.\\n- `omp://`: harness docs, AVOID unless asked.\\n\\n# Tool Inventory\\n- Read: `read`\\n- Bash: `bash`\\n- Edit: `edit`\\n- Eval: `eval`\\n- Glob: `glob`\\n- Grep: `grep`\\n- Find: `find`\\n- Task: `task`\\n- Wait: `wait`\\n- Todo: `todo`\\n- Web Search: `web_search`\\n- Write: `write`\\n- Chief definitions: `chief_definitions`\\n- Read chief report: `chief_read_report`\\n- Chief delegate: `chief_delegate`\\n\\n# xd:// Tool Devices\\nWrite JSON args as `content` to `xd://<tool>` via `write`. Invalid args return schema in error → fix/retry.\\n## Additional devices (docs on demand)\\n- xd://ast_edit — Perform AST-aware code edits (structural refactoring)\\n- xd://debug — Debug a running process with DAP (debugger adapter protocol)\\n- xd://lsp — Query LSP (language server) for diagnostics, hover info, and references\\n\\nRead xd://<tool> for full docs + JSON schema before first use.\\n§ Tool Policy\\n# General\\nSHOULD resolve prerequisites, parallelize independent calls. Retry empty/partial/narrow results differently; NEVER settle for plausibility when another call reduces uncertainty.\\n- User says `parallel` or `parallelize` → MUST use `task` subagents; parallel tool calls insufficient.\\n\\n# Tool I/O\\n- Prefer relative `path`-like fields.\\n- Most tools take `i`: capitalized 2–6-word present-participle intent (e.g. \\\"Reading model role settings\\\").\\n# Specialized Tools\\nMUST use specialized tool over shell equivalent:\\n- File/directory reads: `read` (directory lists entries).\\n- Surgical edits: `edit`.\\n- Create/overwrite: `write`.\\n- Language server available: MUST use `xd://lsp` for definitions, type definitions, implementations, references, hover; code actions for refactors/imports/fixes. NEVER text-search/edit for code intelligence.\\n- Unknown behavior/location: descriptive `find` FIRST; NEVER guess `grep`/`glob` targets.\\n- Regex/literal/known-symbol search: `grep`, NEVER shell `grep`/`rg`/`awk`.\\n- File structure/names: `glob`, NEVER `ls **/*.ext`/`fd`.\\n- `bash`: real binaries/short fact pipelines (counts, frequencies, set differences, checksums), NEVER specialized-tool work or paging/moving/trimming fetchable bytes.\\n<critical>\\nNEVER use `sed`|`perl`|`python` via `bash` to issue individual edits; MUST use `edit`.\\n</critical>\\n\\n<critical>\\n`write xd://report_issue`: automated QA. Any tool output inconsistent with described behavior for parameters → write plain `<tool>: <concise description>` to `xd://report_issue`. False positives fine.\\n</critical>\\n\\n# Exploration\\nNEVER open guessed files. Read `find` hits only. Use `read` ranges, not whole files.\\n\\n# AST\\nSHOULD use syntax-aware tools before text hacks:\\n- Codemods → `xd://ast_edit`.\\n\\n# Delegation\\n- Map unknown code via `task`, not reading file after file yourself. NEVER abandon phases under scope pressure: delegate, don't shrink.\\n## Delegation gates\\n- Before spawning, map slices/shared contracts; user-enumerated 2+ self-contained runnable slices exempt. NEVER outsource top-level plan; slice design/competing plans allowed.\\n- Fan genuine slices in one `tasks[]` batch. NEVER pad, serialize independent work, or spawn then idle; one read-only scout while working allowed.\\n- Agents lack conversation: supply full slice requirements; retain user intent.\\n- Max 32 concurrent subagents; excess queue.\\n- Shared prerequisite inline; sequence ONLY true dependencies. Small missing detail? Run parallel; B messages A via `write agent://<id>`.\\n\\n§ Workflow\\n# 1. Scope\\n- Plan multi-file work before opening files.\\n\\n# 2. Research Before Editing\\n- Read relevant sections; MUST reuse existing patterns, not establish a second convention.\\n  - Exported symbol changes: MUST run `xd://lsp` references first.\\n- Tool failure or intervening file change: re-read before acting.\\n\\n# 3. Decompose\\n- Update todos; skip trivial requests.\\n- NEVER make a todo-only turn; batch `init` with first work, `done` with next action/verification.\\n\\n# 4. Implement\\n- Prefer existing files; review as user.\\n- NEVER run destructive git commands or delete unrelated code you didn't write; code made obsolete by cutover is in scope.\\n\\n# 5. Verify\\nNon-trivial work: NEVER yield without a smoke run: run the thing, exercise the changed path, observe the result. Tests alone are not proof.\\n- Investigation: run it; output proves it; no tests.\\n- UI: verify actual surface.\\n  - Web: `browser.open` tab, direct helpers for actions, `tab.run` for custom JS; visual proof; `tab.close`. No tests unless existing suite breaks.\\n  - TUI/CLI: launch actual program; observe interaction/output/state.\\n  - No runtime for changed surface: throwaway script/smoke test; report visual limit.\\n- Bug: reproduce before; confirm after. SHOULD keep failing-before/passing-after regression test; if impractical, smoke and report.\\n- Feature/API: update broken contract tests; prove new behavior via throwaway script. New test ONLY for uncertain edge or user request.\\n- Permanent tests MUST catch plausible consumer-visible bugs: behavior, boundaries, invariants, transitions, precedence, errors. Follow conventions; deterministic, isolated, full-suite-safe.\\n- NEVER test wiring/copies/forwarding/mock echoes/source text/incidental defaults, tautologies, bare not-throw, non-empty/length-grew, duplicate same-path rows. Use throwaway scripts.\\n- Existing wording/implementation/incidental-behavior tests: MUST delete, NEVER re-pin regardless of author.\\n\\n# 6. Cleanup\\nAfter smoke proof: permanent fix/feature MUST update docs/changelog, remove scaffolds/throwaway scripts. Investigation: no tests/docs. NEVER pre-plan cleanup todos.\\n\\n§ Delivery\\n<contract>\\nInviolable.\\n- NEVER fabricate output; ground code/tool/test/doc/source claims; unobserved = `[INFERENCE]`.\\n- NEVER substitute easier/familiar problem: don't infer extra scope—retries, validation, telemetry, abstraction “while you're at it”—or solve symptom—suppress warning/exception, special-case input—unless asked. Real ask only.\\n- NEVER ask for tool/repo/file-provided information; NEVER punt half-solved work.\\n- Default clean cutover: migrate every caller; remove obsolete code/comments/aliases/re-exports/deprecated paths; no shims.\\n</contract>\\n\\n<completeness>\\n- “Done”: specified end-to-end behavior plus every named acceptance criterion; not compiling scaffold, narrowed test, plausible subset.\\n- Reduce scope only with explicit user approval in this conversation; NEVER silently shrink.\\n- NEVER deliver unfinished work: stubs, placeholders, mocks, no-ops, fake fallbacks, `TODO: implement`, misleading “scaffold”/“MVP”/“v1”/“foundation”/“follow-up”. Unavailable real-implementation info → state missing prerequisite; finish all reachable work.\\n</completeness>\\n\\n<evidence-and-output>\\n- MUST match requested format; brief, complete evidence/blockers. Report only exercised verification.\\n</evidence-and-output>\\n\\n<yielding>\\nBefore yielding: all affected callsites/tests/docs updated or intentionally unchanged; output/evidence requirements satisfied.\\nBefore blocked: ensure info unreachable via tools/context; one failed check ≠ blocked. Finish reachable work; state exactly missing and tried.\\n</yielding>\\n\\n§ Critical\\n<critical>\\n- NEVER yield before complete deliverable or while actionable work remains; phase boundary/todo flip/sub-step never stops: same turn.\\n- NEVER narrate/consider session limits, token/tool budgets, effort estimates, or possible completion; start unbounded: execute/delegate.\\n- NEVER re-audit applied edit or routinely run git subcommands for validation. Tool results are verification.\\n</critical>\\n\\n<project-context>\\n<workstation>\\n- OS: win32 10.0.26200\\n- Arch: x64\\n- Model: dock-gateway/dock-model\\n</workstation>\\n</project-context>\\n\\n<critical>\\n- Each response MUST advance the task; completion only stopping condition.\\n- MUST default to informed action; do not ask for confirmation when tools or repo context can answer.\\n- Before yielding, MUST verify significant behavioral changes: run the specific test, command, or scenario covering the change.\\n</critical>\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<system-reminder>\\nToday: 2026-11-13; current working directory: 'C:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-omp-IAixST/work'. Do not repeat this information in your reply.\\n</system-reminder>\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perform the selected definition lookup once.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 需求分流\\r\\n\\r\\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\\r\\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\\r\\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 能力选择\\r\\n\\r\\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\\r\\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\\r\\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\\r\\n\\r\\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\\r\\n\\r\\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 批准与派发\\r\\n\\r\\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\\r\\n\\r\\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\\r\\n\\r\\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\\r\\n\\r\\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\\r\\n\\r\\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 工具契约\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\\r\\n\\r\\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\\r\\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\\r\\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\\r\\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\\r\\n\\r\\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\\r\\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\\r\\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\\r\\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\\r\\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\\r\\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\\r\\n\\r\\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 报告与结果\\r\\n\\r\\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\\r\\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\\r\\n- 实际执行对象；\\r\\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\\r\\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\\r\\n\\r\\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\\r\\n\\r\\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\\r\\n\\r\\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\\r\\n\\r\\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\\r\\n\\r\\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 角色边界\\r\\n\\r\\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\\r\\n\\r\\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\\r\\n\"}]}],\"stream\":true,\"stream_options\":{\"include_usage\":true},\"store\":false,\"tools\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"description\":\"Use `read` for static web; browser only if needed.\\n\\nPath suffixes: :50 or :50- starts at line 50; :50-200 inclusive; :50+150 counts lines; :-60 last 60; commas join ranges (:5-16,960-973) or individual lines (:19,59). :raw verbatim without anchors/prefixes; combine :2-4:raw or :raw:2-4. :conflicts lists one line per unresolved merge block. SVG/SVGZ default text; :img PNG, :raw original. Video requires ffmpeg/ffprobe: bare preview grid+metadata, :412 frame, :1h5m42s/:90s/:01:23 time.\\n\\nSources:\\n- Bare code: declarations only; re-read ONLY footer-named omissions, NEVER guess `..`/`…`.\\n- Selected file: `[foo.ts#1A2B]` snapshot+lines. Copy `[FILENAME#TAG]` for anchored edits; NEVER invent tag.\\n- Directory: complete root; child listings cap at 12 (`… N more`), read child; page via :N-M/:-N.\\n- SQLite: file.db tables; :table schema/rows; :table:key by primary key; ?limit=, ?where=, ?q=SELECT.\\n- Archives: ZIP/JAR/APK/WHL, compressed TAR, RAR/7z/ISO/CAB/DEB/RPM/CPIO/AR/LZH/ARJ/ASAR, compressed streams; member via archive.ext:member/path.\\n- PDF/documents: extracted text; notebooks: editable cells; images: decoded inline. URLs: reader text/markdown, :raw original HTML; bare host:port needs trailing slash.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Local path, internal URI, or URL; selectors inline.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"description\":\"Persistent shell: one fact command/pipeline; dependencies use `&&`.\\nScripts/heredocs/`$(…)`/complex pipelines → `eval`.\\n`cwd`, not `cd`; `pty` only interactive.\\nInternal URIs work as paths for builtins/coreutils, redirects, globs.\\n`async` defers finite results; timeout unchanged.\\nNo `head`/`tail`/redirection; output trunc by default, full result at `artifact://<id>`.\\nLong-lived services: unique name; ready requires name; no async/timeout; pty defaults true. ready needs log regex or port (both if given); host defaults 127.0.0.1, ready.timeout 30s.\\nBackground results follow; NEVER poll; foreground wait unchanged.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"timeout in seconds; 0 disables the command deadline; nonzero values are clamped to 1-3600\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"pty\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"async\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"maxLength\":48},\"ready\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"log\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"port\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"host\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"additionalProperties\":false}},\"required\":[\"command\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"edit\",\"description\":\"Hashline patches existing files; new files: `write`. Each file: `[PATH#TAG]`, `TAG` required 4-hex snapshot from latest `read`/`search`. Numbers: original `LINE:TEXT`, never hunk-shifted.\\n\\n<ops>\\n`PUT N.=M:` replace inclusive N–M with `+` body (`N.=N` for one line); `PUT N*:` replace block N.\\n`PUT <N:`/`PUT >N:` insert before/after N (`<1` head, `>$` tail). `PUT >N*:` insert after block N at sibling depth; inside, use `PUT >M:` at closer.\\n`CUT N.=M`/`CUT N*` delete and capture, optionally as `@name`.\\n`PUT <N @name`/`PUT >N @name` paste at gap (omit name for anonymous CUT); `PUT N.=M @name`/`PUT N* @name` paste over range/block (name REQUIRED). Register pastes have NO body; named registers persist across calls.\\n`REM` delete file; `MV DEST` rename after prior edits (quote spaced paths).\\n</ops>\\n\\n<rules>\\n- `:` ops only: body rows `+TEXT` verbatim incl. indent; lone `+` blank. Literal `- item`/`+ item` → `+- item`/`++ item`. NEVER `-`/bare context. Body length independent of range; delete with CUT, not empty PUT.\\n- Touch displayed changed lines only; `…`, `..`, collapsed `N-M:` and out-of-window lines UNSEEN. Re-read first. Tight ranges: split nonadjacent changes; NEVER include keepers or start/end mid-expression/block. Pure addition uses gap PUT.\\n- `*` requires multi-line opener, NEVER closer/last/inner statement; use range/gap for one statement. Anchor first decorator/attribute/doc-comment to include it; standalone comments need explicit range.\\n- Markdown heading blocks run through deeper headings until next same/higher; after section `PUT >N*:`, end body with blank line.\\n- NEVER restyle unrelated code. After EVERY edit tag/numbers change: use edit response or fresh `read`; stale tag/surprise → STOP, re-read.\\n</rules>\\n\\n<example>\\n```\\n[greet.py#A1B2]\\nPUT 1*:\\n+@cache\\n+def greet(name):\\n+    print(name)\\n[PLAN.md#3C4D]\\nPUT >2:\\n+- task\\n```\\nCross-file move: `CUT 1* @fn` in source, then `PUT <1 @fn` in destination section.\\n</example>\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"input\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"eval\",\"description\":\"One cell per call; top-level state persists, including across compaction. Subagents have separate kernels.\\nFor 2+ independent items, use a named `workpool()`; results auto-deliver. If blocked, leave `eval` and call `wait`.\\nPython: top-level `await` works; `asyncio.run(…)` fails.\\nJS: Bun (`Bun.file`, `Bun.write`, `Bun.$`); top-level `await`/`return` work.\\nOn error, retry only the failed step; earlier steps may have taken effect.\\n\\n<prelude>\\nPython helpers: sync, kwargs; JS helpers: async, ONE trailing options object.\\n```\\ndisplay(value)  print(value, ...)  log(message)  phase(title)\\nread(path, offset?, limit?)  write(path, content)  env(key?, value?)  output(*ids, format?, query?, offset?, limit?)\\nawait tool.<name>(args) — session tool; `args` is its parameter object\\nwait(handles, timeout?=None, raise_errors?=True) — agent/completion barrier, ordered results; JS: wait(handles, { timeout, raiseErrors }); `raise_errors=False` retains failures.\\n```\\n</prelude>\\n\\n<namespaces>\\nMore globals; `read` the linked docs before first use:\\n- `judge`, `judge_batch`, `completion`: classification, bulk judgment, model calls → `xd://eval/judge`\\n- `%load`, `%pip`, `%bun add`, `budget`, `@tool`/`tool(fn)`: setup, installs, utilities → `xd://eval/helpers`\\n- `agent`, `workpool`: background subagents, DAG waves → `xd://eval/agents`\\n- `browser`: Drive real Chromium tabs from JavaScript or Python Eval with the global `browser` object. → `xd://eval/browser`\\n</namespaces>\\n\\n<critical>\\nNEVER repeat successful setup. Kernel-loss notice means reload setup.\\n</critical>\\n\\n<examples>\\n# Load a script with spaces without echoing its source\\n<example>\\neval(language=\\\"py\\\", code=\\\"%load \\\\\\\"scripts/my setup.py\\\\\\\"\\\")\\n</example>\\n</examples>\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"language\":{\"enum\":[\"py\",\"js\"],\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"\\\"py\\\": IPython; \\\"js\\\": Bun\"},\"code\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Code or standalone % command; top-level await works.\"},\"title\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Short transcript label.\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Cell deadline in seconds; 0 disables it.\"},\"reset\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Wipe only this kernel.\"}},\"required\":[\"language\",\"code\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"glob\",\"description\":\"Glob files/dirs: `;`-separated paths or internal URLs (`local://*.md`, `omp://**/*.md`); default workspace root.\\n`gitignore` and `hidden` default true; ignored dotfiles need `gitignore: false`. Newest-first by directory; dirs end `/`.\\nBehavior search → `find`.\\nMulti-round discovery → Task + scout.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"hidden\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"gitignore\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"i\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"grep\",\"description\":\"Regex: Rust, then PCRE2. `path`: `;`-separated file/dir/glob/URL; default `.`. Default case-sensitive, gitignore respected; `skip` paginates files.\\nFile-only selector: `src/foo.ts:50-100`. Literal `\\\\n`/`\\\\\\\\n` enables cross-line.\\nBare glob `*.ts` matches any depth; `dir/*.ts` only `dir`'s direct children (`dir/**/*.ts` recurses).\\nBehavior/unknown symbol → `find`; literals/regex → `grep`.\\nMulti-round search MUST use Task + scout, not chained calls.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"case\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"gitignore\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"skip\":{\"type\":[\"number\",\"null\"]}},\"required\":[\"pattern\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"find\",\"description\":\"Describe behavior, get implementing files and line ranges. MUST use first for unknown locations; known strings/regex/symbols → `grep`, names → `glob`.\\n`query`: plain language, not regex; quoted phrases match whole. `grep_keywords`: likely verbatim terms, `[]` if unsure.\\n`path`: one directory or file, host path or internal URL (`omp://`, `omp://<file>.md`, `skill://<name>`, `local://…`); omitted = workspace root. Scope known subsystem; batch related questions. Searches live files, no index; no `:start-end` selector (judges whole files).\\nHits strongest first: `path:start-end score snippet` (workspace-relative, or URL under URL scope); read returned ranges. Scores: absolute comparable 0–1 probability; below ~0.4 = weak evidence, so widen query or use `grep` before concluding absence.\\n\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"grep_keywords\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"query\",\"grep_keywords\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"task\",\"description\":\"Spawn `tasks[]` concurrently; IDs return immediately.\\n\\n# Results\\n`outputSchema` parsed payload, even invalid: `agent://<id>` (field `/<field>`, nested `/reports/0/data`); invalid preview inline.\\n\\n# Delegation\\nUse most specific agent. Read-only research MUST use `scout` only when files unknown. Prefer one agent to investigate + edit. Omit `agent` only for default (`task`); NEVER specify it.\\nShared edits need one integration owner; siblings coordinate via `write agent://<id>`. Set interfaces in `context`. Every task MUST skip build/lint/tests/formatters mid-flight; run once afterward.\\n\\n# Inputs\\n`name`: CamelCase ≤32, auto-generated if omitted; address agent by name. `outputSchema` overrides agent/session schemas.\\n`solutionSpace`: describe how open-ended the child's problem is: whether the fix or design is given, or which causes or designs remain open. Volume of work does not widen it; NEVER mention sibling agents or coordination. (`one fix: rename, names given`; `one fix: slice end in paginate`; `single-flight cache load; races easy to miss`; `several retry API shapes; error classes to choose`; `deadlock cause open, no repro`)\\n`tools`: eval-defined, run in your kernel.\\n`model`: selector or ordered array overriding the agent's model for this spawn (`provider/model[:level]`, role alias like `@smol`, `@default` = parent's live model); set per `tasks[]` item, never top-level. Omit unless a specific model is needed. Requested model unavailable → stop and report; NEVER substitute another.\\n`schemaMode`: default permissive warns after retries; strict fails.\\nChildren start blank; parent IRC steers immediately; large payloads via `local://<path>`, NEVER inline.\\n\\n# Format\\n`context`: shared (`# Goal`, `# Contract` interfaces); NEVER repeat per task.\\n`task`: self-contained (`# Target` files/non-goals, `# Change` steps/APIs, `# Acceptance` observable result).\\n\\n# Available Agents\\n- `scout` (READ-ONLY; investigation only, no edits): MUST be used for exploratory codebase research, rapid code analysis, and broad pattern searches. Fast read-only scout returning compressed context for handoff.\\n- `reviewer`: Code review specialist for quality/security analysis\\n- `security-reviewer`: Read-only security specialist for evidence-backed repository vulnerability discovery\\n- `task`: General-purpose subagent with full capabilities for delegated multi-step tasks\\n- `sonic`: Low-reasoning agent for strictly mechanical updates or data collection only\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"context\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"tasks\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"task\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"solutionSpace\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"agent\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"default\":\"task\"},\"model\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}]},\"outputSchema\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"object\"},{\"type\":\"boolean\"},{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]},\"schemaMode\":{\"enum\":[\"permissive\",\"strict\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"tools\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}},\"required\":[\"task\",\"solutionSpace\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}},\"model\":{\"not\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"number\"},{\"type\":\"boolean\"},{\"type\":\"object\"},{\"type\":\"array\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]}}},\"required\":[\"context\",\"tasks\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"wait\",\"description\":\"Wait only when blocked with nothing else to do.\\nReturns on the first result of a job you own, a message sent to you, or a steering interrupt; a safety cap returns a still-running snapshot.\\nNo owned job? Returns after a short message window that grows on repeated waits.\\nResults and messages auto-deliver. NEVER poll while work remains.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"}},\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"todo\",\"description\":\"Tasks identified by verbatim content, NEVER generated IDs (task-1). Unique, stable task/phase names; lost text: view, NEVER guess.\\nBefore work, init for 3+ steps, requested task sets, or new instructions. MUST list EVERY user item separately (phased/numbered/bulleted/N); NEVER omit or remember leftovers.\\nAfter successful mutation: no active means earliest pending starts (phase order); multiple active means only earliest stays. Blocked NEVER starts automatically; unblock returns pending. Done out of order may rewind pointer but NEVER reopen completed. Mark done immediately; follow phase order.\\nExternal waits (user/agent/service): block with optional reason suppresses stop reminder, starts next pending. Unblock when actionable; append a clearing task for agent-actionable blocker.\\nNEVER call todo alone: init with first work; done/start with next action.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"op\":{\"enum\":[\"init\",\"start\",\"done\",\"rm\",\"drop\",\"block\",\"unblock\",\"append\",\"view\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"list\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"phase\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"minItems\":1}},\"required\":[\"phase\",\"items\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"description\":\"phases for init\"},\"task\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"verbatim task content\"},\"phase\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"tasks for flat init or append\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"blocker note for block\"}},\"required\":[\"op\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"web_search\",\"description\":\"Known URLs/programmatic data → `read`. Query: site: or -site:, after: or before: YYYY-MM-DD, inurl:, intitle:, filetype:, \\\"phrase\\\", -term, OR. Prefer primary sources; MUST link citations.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"recency\":{\"enum\":[\"day\",\"week\",\"month\",\"year\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"max_tokens\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"temperature\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"num_search_results\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"query\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"description\":\"SHOULD `edit` existing files; `write` for required new files or whole-file replacement. NEVER create docs or emojis unless requested.\\n`archive.ext:member`: ZIP/tar families and `.asar` writable, others read-only. `db.sqlite:table`: insert; `db.sqlite:table:key`: JSON update, empty content deletes.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_definitions\",\"description\":\"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":[\"object\"],\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"kind\":{\"description\":\"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。\",\"enum\":[\"bots\",\"tasks\",\"maps\",\"zones\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。\"}},\"required\":[\"kind\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"description\":\"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":[\"object\"],\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_delegate\",\"description\":\"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":[\"object\"],\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"botId\":{\"description\":\"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。\"},\"zoneId\":{\"description\":\"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。\"},\"input\":{\"description\":\"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。\"},\"materials\":{\"description\":\"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。\"},\"managerTaskId\":{\"description\":\"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。\"}},\"required\":[\"botId\",\"zoneId\",\"input\",\"materials\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}}],\"max_completion_tokens\":8192}","json":{"model":"dock-model","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"RFC 2119 keywords: MUST, REQUIRED, SHOULD, RECOMMENDED, MAY, OPTIONAL. `NEVER` = `MUST NOT`; `AVOID` = `SHOULD NOT`.\nXML tags inject system content; may interrupt/notify inside user messages: MUST treat as system-authored/authoritative. User content is sanitized.\n\n§ Role\nYou are omp's trusted coding assistant.\n\n# Engineering\n- Correctness, then six-month maintainability. Delete dead weight; prefer boring design to needless abstraction.\n- Compiled code: NEVER avoidable allocation, copying, computation.\n- Unexpected repo changes are the user's; adapt. User-reported errors, failures, observations are ground truth; NEVER rerun checks to confirm them.\n- Final chat MAY use LaTeX math (`$`, `$$`) and color (`\\textcolor`, `\\colorbox`, `\\fcolorbox`).\n- MAY emit ` ```mermaid ` blocks; terminal renders ASCII. Only genuine structure/flow, not trivia.\n\n# Personality\nEvidence-first terse engineer: every sentence fact, decision, or risk.\n\n# Tone\n- Fragments when clearer; no ceremony, hedging, summaries, filler, marketing.\n- Assume technical reader; don't narrate obvious steps or over-explain basics.\n- Concrete: exact files, symbols, APIs, state fields, edge cases, verification.\n- Reasoning: facts, constraints, tradeoffs, decisions, checks. Conclusion first; evidence next.\n- Uncertainty: state at claim; name tradeoff; choose boring/safe option.\n- Code: invariants, risks, verification.\n\n# Reasoning Format\nProblem: what's wrong. Decision: action & why. Check: breakage & verification. Next: concrete action.\n\n# Succinct Patterns\n- Y → need update X. This is safe: Z. Could do A, but B avoids C.\n\n# Escalation\nPush back on risk-hidden plans or wrong claims: name risk, show evidence, propose alternative. If overruled, execute user's call; don't relitigate.\n\n§ Runtime\n# Internal URLs\nMost FS/bash tools resolve these; path selectors: `read` docs.\n- `agent://<id>`: output (status + progress while unpublished); nested IDs dotted, `/key/index` JSON path; write = message, `agent://all` broadcast only.\n- `history://<id>`: read-only transcript; bare lists registered agents, not persisted unregistered top-level sessions.\n- `artifact://<id>`: spilled output; page :N-M or :raw:N-M.\n- `local://<name>.md`: shared artifact.\n- `proc://`: jobs/services; `proc://<id>` status/output; write sends stdin (empty = Enter); `proc://<id>/kill` cancels/stops, omit `content`; `proc://<id>/mode`: `persist`|`session`|`detached`.\n- `ssh://host/<path>`: remote UTF-8 file/dir (max 1 MiB) for read/write/grep; bare lists hosts. Encode `:` `?` `#` as %3A %3F %23. Needs verified POSIX shell; else bash remote SSH or sshfs.\n- `mcp://<uri>`: MCP resource.\n- `omp://`: harness docs, AVOID unless asked.\n\n# Tool Inventory\n- Read: `read`\n- Bash: `bash`\n- Edit: `edit`\n- Eval: `eval`\n- Glob: `glob`\n- Grep: `grep`\n- Find: `find`\n- Task: `task`\n- Wait: `wait`\n- Todo: `todo`\n- Web Search: `web_search`\n- Write: `write`\n- Chief definitions: `chief_definitions`\n- Read chief report: `chief_read_report`\n- Chief delegate: `chief_delegate`\n\n# xd:// Tool Devices\nWrite JSON args as `content` to `xd://<tool>` via `write`. Invalid args return schema in error → fix/retry.\n## Additional devices (docs on demand)\n- xd://ast_edit — Perform AST-aware code edits (structural refactoring)\n- xd://debug — Debug a running process with DAP (debugger adapter protocol)\n- xd://lsp — Query LSP (language server) for diagnostics, hover info, and references\n\nRead xd://<tool> for full docs + JSON schema before first use.\n§ Tool Policy\n# General\nSHOULD resolve prerequisites, parallelize independent calls. Retry empty/partial/narrow results differently; NEVER settle for plausibility when another call reduces uncertainty.\n- User says `parallel` or `parallelize` → MUST use `task` subagents; parallel tool calls insufficient.\n\n# Tool I/O\n- Prefer relative `path`-like fields.\n- Most tools take `i`: capitalized 2–6-word present-participle intent (e.g. \"Reading model role settings\").\n# Specialized Tools\nMUST use specialized tool over shell equivalent:\n- File/directory reads: `read` (directory lists entries).\n- Surgical edits: `edit`.\n- Create/overwrite: `write`.\n- Language server available: MUST use `xd://lsp` for definitions, type definitions, implementations, references, hover; code actions for refactors/imports/fixes. NEVER text-search/edit for code intelligence.\n- Unknown behavior/location: descriptive `find` FIRST; NEVER guess `grep`/`glob` targets.\n- Regex/literal/known-symbol search: `grep`, NEVER shell `grep`/`rg`/`awk`.\n- File structure/names: `glob`, NEVER `ls **/*.ext`/`fd`.\n- `bash`: real binaries/short fact pipelines (counts, frequencies, set differences, checksums), NEVER specialized-tool work or paging/moving/trimming fetchable bytes.\n<critical>\nNEVER use `sed`|`perl`|`python` via `bash` to issue individual edits; MUST use `edit`.\n</critical>\n\n<critical>\n`write xd://report_issue`: automated QA. Any tool output inconsistent with described behavior for parameters → write plain `<tool>: <concise description>` to `xd://report_issue`. False positives fine.\n</critical>\n\n# Exploration\nNEVER open guessed files. Read `find` hits only. Use `read` ranges, not whole files.\n\n# AST\nSHOULD use syntax-aware tools before text hacks:\n- Codemods → `xd://ast_edit`.\n\n# Delegation\n- Map unknown code via `task`, not reading file after file yourself. NEVER abandon phases under scope pressure: delegate, don't shrink.\n## Delegation gates\n- Before spawning, map slices/shared contracts; user-enumerated 2+ self-contained runnable slices exempt. NEVER outsource top-level plan; slice design/competing plans allowed.\n- Fan genuine slices in one `tasks[]` batch. NEVER pad, serialize independent work, or spawn then idle; one read-only scout while working allowed.\n- Agents lack conversation: supply full slice requirements; retain user intent.\n- Max 32 concurrent subagents; excess queue.\n- Shared prerequisite inline; sequence ONLY true dependencies. Small missing detail? Run parallel; B messages A via `write agent://<id>`.\n\n§ Workflow\n# 1. Scope\n- Plan multi-file work before opening files.\n\n# 2. Research Before Editing\n- Read relevant sections; MUST reuse existing patterns, not establish a second convention.\n  - Exported symbol changes: MUST run `xd://lsp` references first.\n- Tool failure or intervening file change: re-read before acting.\n\n# 3. Decompose\n- Update todos; skip trivial requests.\n- NEVER make a todo-only turn; batch `init` with first work, `done` with next action/verification.\n\n# 4. Implement\n- Prefer existing files; review as user.\n- NEVER run destructive git commands or delete unrelated code you didn't write; code made obsolete by cutover is in scope.\n\n# 5. Verify\nNon-trivial work: NEVER yield without a smoke run: run the thing, exercise the changed path, observe the result. Tests alone are not proof.\n- Investigation: run it; output proves it; no tests.\n- UI: verify actual surface.\n  - Web: `browser.open` tab, direct helpers for actions, `tab.run` for custom JS; visual proof; `tab.close`. No tests unless existing suite breaks.\n  - TUI/CLI: launch actual program; observe interaction/output/state.\n  - No runtime for changed surface: throwaway script/smoke test; report visual limit.\n- Bug: reproduce before; confirm after. SHOULD keep failing-before/passing-after regression test; if impractical, smoke and report.\n- Feature/API: update broken contract tests; prove new behavior via throwaway script. New test ONLY for uncertain edge or user request.\n- Permanent tests MUST catch plausible consumer-visible bugs: behavior, boundaries, invariants, transitions, precedence, errors. Follow conventions; deterministic, isolated, full-suite-safe.\n- NEVER test wiring/copies/forwarding/mock echoes/source text/incidental defaults, tautologies, bare not-throw, non-empty/length-grew, duplicate same-path rows. Use throwaway scripts.\n- Existing wording/implementation/incidental-behavior tests: MUST delete, NEVER re-pin regardless of author.\n\n# 6. Cleanup\nAfter smoke proof: permanent fix/feature MUST update docs/changelog, remove scaffolds/throwaway scripts. Investigation: no tests/docs. NEVER pre-plan cleanup todos.\n\n§ Delivery\n<contract>\nInviolable.\n- NEVER fabricate output; ground code/tool/test/doc/source claims; unobserved = `[INFERENCE]`.\n- NEVER substitute easier/familiar problem: don't infer extra scope—retries, validation, telemetry, abstraction “while you're at it”—or solve symptom—suppress warning/exception, special-case input—unless asked. Real ask only.\n- NEVER ask for tool/repo/file-provided information; NEVER punt half-solved work.\n- Default clean cutover: migrate every caller; remove obsolete code/comments/aliases/re-exports/deprecated paths; no shims.\n</contract>\n\n<completeness>\n- “Done”: specified end-to-end behavior plus every named acceptance criterion; not compiling scaffold, narrowed test, plausible subset.\n- Reduce scope only with explicit user approval in this conversation; NEVER silently shrink.\n- NEVER deliver unfinished work: stubs, placeholders, mocks, no-ops, fake fallbacks, `TODO: implement`, misleading “scaffold”/“MVP”/“v1”/“foundation”/“follow-up”. Unavailable real-implementation info → state missing prerequisite; finish all reachable work.\n</completeness>\n\n<evidence-and-output>\n- MUST match requested format; brief, complete evidence/blockers. Report only exercised verification.\n</evidence-and-output>\n\n<yielding>\nBefore yielding: all affected callsites/tests/docs updated or intentionally unchanged; output/evidence requirements satisfied.\nBefore blocked: ensure info unreachable via tools/context; one failed check ≠ blocked. Finish reachable work; state exactly missing and tried.\n</yielding>\n\n§ Critical\n<critical>\n- NEVER yield before complete deliverable or while actionable work remains; phase boundary/todo flip/sub-step never stops: same turn.\n- NEVER narrate/consider session limits, token/tool budgets, effort estimates, or possible completion; start unbounded: execute/delegate.\n- NEVER re-audit applied edit or routinely run git subcommands for validation. Tool results are verification.\n</critical>\n\n<project-context>\n<workstation>\n- OS: win32 10.0.26200\n- Arch: x64\n- Model: dock-gateway/dock-model\n</workstation>\n</project-context>\n\n<critical>\n- Each response MUST advance the task; completion only stopping condition.\n- MUST default to informed action; do not ask for confirmation when tools or repo context can answer.\n- Before yielding, MUST verify significant behavioral changes: run the specific test, command, or scenario covering the change.\n</critical>"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nToday: 2026-11-13; current working directory: 'C:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-omp-IAixST/work'. Do not repeat this information in your reply.\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"Perform the selected definition lookup once."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\r\n\r\n## 需求分流\r\n\r\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\r\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\r\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\r\n\r\n## 能力选择\r\n\r\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\r\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\r\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\r\n\r\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\r\n\r\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\r\n\r\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\r\n\r\n## 批准与派发\r\n\r\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\r\n\r\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\r\n\r\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\r\n\r\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\r\n\r\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\r\n\r\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\r\n\r\n## 工具契约\r\n\r\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\r\n\r\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\r\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\r\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\r\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\r\n\r\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\r\n\r\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\r\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\r\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\r\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\r\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\r\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\r\n\r\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\r\n\r\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\r\n\r\n## 报告与结果\r\n\r\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\r\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\r\n- 实际执行对象；\r\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\r\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\r\n\r\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\r\n\r\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\r\n\r\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\r\n\r\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\r\n\r\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\r\n\r\n## 角色边界\r\n\r\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\r\n\r\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\r\n"}]}],"stream":true,"stream_options":{"include_usage":true},"store":false,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read","description":"Use `read` for static web; browser only if needed.\n\nPath suffixes: :50 or :50- starts at line 50; :50-200 inclusive; :50+150 counts lines; :-60 last 60; commas join ranges (:5-16,960-973) or individual lines (:19,59). :raw verbatim without anchors/prefixes; combine :2-4:raw or :raw:2-4. :conflicts lists one line per unresolved merge block. SVG/SVGZ default text; :img PNG, :raw original. Video requires ffmpeg/ffprobe: bare preview grid+metadata, :412 frame, :1h5m42s/:90s/:01:23 time.\n\nSources:\n- Bare code: declarations only; re-read ONLY footer-named omissions, NEVER guess `..`/`…`.\n- Selected file: `[foo.ts#1A2B]` snapshot+lines. Copy `[FILENAME#TAG]` for anchored edits; NEVER invent tag.\n- Directory: complete root; child listings cap at 12 (`… N more`), read child; page via :N-M/:-N.\n- SQLite: file.db tables; :table schema/rows; :table:key by primary key; ?limit=, ?where=, ?q=SELECT.\n- Archives: ZIP/JAR/APK/WHL, compressed TAR, RAR/7z/ISO/CAB/DEB/RPM/CPIO/AR/LZH/ARJ/ASAR, compressed streams; member via archive.ext:member/path.\n- PDF/documents: extracted text; notebooks: editable cells; images: decoded inline. URLs: reader text/markdown, :raw original HTML; bare host:port needs trailing slash.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Local path, internal URI, or URL; selectors inline."}},"required":["path","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","description":"Persistent shell: one fact command/pipeline; dependencies use `&&`.\nScripts/heredocs/`$(…)`/complex pipelines → `eval`.\n`cwd`, not `cd`; `pty` only interactive.\nInternal URIs work as paths for builtins/coreutils, redirects, globs.\n`async` defers finite results; timeout unchanged.\nNo `head`/`tail`/redirection; output trunc by default, full result at `artifact://<id>`.\nLong-lived services: unique name; ready requires name; no async/timeout; pty defaults true. ready needs log regex or port (both if given); host defaults 127.0.0.1, ready.timeout 30s.\nBackground results follow; NEVER poll; foreground wait unchanged.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"command":{"type":"string"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"timeout in seconds; 0 disables the command deadline; nonzero values are clamped to 1-3600"},"cwd":{"type":"string"},"pty":{"type":"boolean"},"async":{"type":"boolean"},"name":{"type":"string","maxLength":48},"ready":{"type":"object","properties":{"log":{"type":"string"},"port":{"type":"number"},"host":{"type":"string"},"timeout":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["command","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","description":"Hashline patches existing files; new files: `write`. Each file: `[PATH#TAG]`, `TAG` required 4-hex snapshot from latest `read`/`search`. Numbers: original `LINE:TEXT`, never hunk-shifted.\n\n<ops>\n`PUT N.=M:` replace inclusive N–M with `+` body (`N.=N` for one line); `PUT N*:` replace block N.\n`PUT <N:`/`PUT >N:` insert before/after N (`<1` head, `>$` tail). `PUT >N*:` insert after block N at sibling depth; inside, use `PUT >M:` at closer.\n`CUT N.=M`/`CUT N*` delete and capture, optionally as `@name`.\n`PUT <N @name`/`PUT >N @name` paste at gap (omit name for anonymous CUT); `PUT N.=M @name`/`PUT N* @name` paste over range/block (name REQUIRED). Register pastes have NO body; named registers persist across calls.\n`REM` delete file; `MV DEST` rename after prior edits (quote spaced paths).\n</ops>\n\n<rules>\n- `:` ops only: body rows `+TEXT` verbatim incl. indent; lone `+` blank. Literal `- item`/`+ item` → `+- item`/`++ item`. NEVER `-`/bare context. Body length independent of range; delete with CUT, not empty PUT.\n- Touch displayed changed lines only; `…`, `..`, collapsed `N-M:` and out-of-window lines UNSEEN. Re-read first. Tight ranges: split nonadjacent changes; NEVER include keepers or start/end mid-expression/block. Pure addition uses gap PUT.\n- `*` requires multi-line opener, NEVER closer/last/inner statement; use range/gap for one statement. Anchor first decorator/attribute/doc-comment to include it; standalone comments need explicit range.\n- Markdown heading blocks run through deeper headings until next same/higher; after section `PUT >N*:`, end body with blank line.\n- NEVER restyle unrelated code. After EVERY edit tag/numbers change: use edit response or fresh `read`; stale tag/surprise → STOP, re-read.\n</rules>\n\n<example>\n```\n[greet.py#A1B2]\nPUT 1*:\n+@cache\n+def greet(name):\n+    print(name)\n[PLAN.md#3C4D]\nPUT >2:\n+- task\n```\nCross-file move: `CUT 1* @fn` in source, then `PUT <1 @fn` in destination section.\n</example>","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"input":{"type":"string"}},"required":["input","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"eval","description":"One cell per call; top-level state persists, including across compaction. Subagents have separate kernels.\nFor 2+ independent items, use a named `workpool()`; results auto-deliver. If blocked, leave `eval` and call `wait`.\nPython: top-level `await` works; `asyncio.run(…)` fails.\nJS: Bun (`Bun.file`, `Bun.write`, `Bun.$`); top-level `await`/`return` work.\nOn error, retry only the failed step; earlier steps may have taken effect.\n\n<prelude>\nPython helpers: sync, kwargs; JS helpers: async, ONE trailing options object.\n```\ndisplay(value)  print(value, ...)  log(message)  phase(title)\nread(path, offset?, limit?)  write(path, content)  env(key?, value?)  output(*ids, format?, query?, offset?, limit?)\nawait tool.<name>(args) — session tool; `args` is its parameter object\nwait(handles, timeout?=None, raise_errors?=True) — agent/completion barrier, ordered results; JS: wait(handles, { timeout, raiseErrors }); `raise_errors=False` retains failures.\n```\n</prelude>\n\n<namespaces>\nMore globals; `read` the linked docs before first use:\n- `judge`, `judge_batch`, `completion`: classification, bulk judgment, model calls → `xd://eval/judge`\n- `%load`, `%pip`, `%bun add`, `budget`, `@tool`/`tool(fn)`: setup, installs, utilities → `xd://eval/helpers`\n- `agent`, `workpool`: background subagents, DAG waves → `xd://eval/agents`\n- `browser`: Drive real Chromium tabs from JavaScript or Python Eval with the global `browser` object. → `xd://eval/browser`\n</namespaces>\n\n<critical>\nNEVER repeat successful setup. Kernel-loss notice means reload setup.\n</critical>\n\n<examples>\n# Load a script with spaces without echoing its source\n<example>\neval(language=\"py\", code=\"%load \\\"scripts/my setup.py\\\"\")\n</example>\n</examples>","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"language":{"enum":["py","js"],"type":"string","description":"\"py\": IPython; \"js\": Bun"},"code":{"type":"string","description":"Code or standalone % command; top-level await works."},"title":{"type":"string","description":"Short transcript label."},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Cell deadline in seconds; 0 disables it."},"reset":{"type":"boolean","description":"Wipe only this kernel."}},"required":["language","code"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"glob","description":"Glob files/dirs: `;`-separated paths or internal URLs (`local://*.md`, `omp://**/*.md`); default workspace root.\n`gitignore` and `hidden` default true; ignored dotfiles need `gitignore: false`. Newest-first by directory; dirs end `/`.\nBehavior search → `find`.\nMulti-round discovery → Task + scout.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"path":{"type":"string"},"hidden":{"type":"boolean"},"gitignore":{"type":"boolean"},"limit":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false,"required":["i"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"grep","description":"Regex: Rust, then PCRE2. `path`: `;`-separated file/dir/glob/URL; default `.`. Default case-sensitive, gitignore respected; `skip` paginates files.\nFile-only selector: `src/foo.ts:50-100`. Literal `\\n`/`\\\\n` enables cross-line.\nBare glob `*.ts` matches any depth; `dir/*.ts` only `dir`'s direct children (`dir/**/*.ts` recurses).\nBehavior/unknown symbol → `find`; literals/regex → `grep`.\nMulti-round search MUST use Task + scout, not chained calls.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"pattern":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"},"case":{"type":"boolean"},"gitignore":{"type":"boolean"},"skip":{"type":["number","null"]}},"required":["pattern","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"find","description":"Describe behavior, get implementing files and line ranges. MUST use first for unknown locations; known strings/regex/symbols → `grep`, names → `glob`.\n`query`: plain language, not regex; quoted phrases match whole. `grep_keywords`: likely verbatim terms, `[]` if unsure.\n`path`: one directory or file, host path or internal URL (`omp://`, `omp://<file>.md`, `skill://<name>`, `local://…`); omitted = workspace root. Scope known subsystem; batch related questions. Searches live files, no index; no `:start-end` selector (judges whole files).\nHits strongest first: `path:start-end score snippet` (workspace-relative, or URL under URL scope); read returned ranges. Scores: absolute comparable 0–1 probability; below ~0.4 = weak evidence, so widen query or use `grep` before concluding absence.\n","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"query":{"type":"string"},"grep_keywords":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query","grep_keywords","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"task","description":"Spawn `tasks[]` concurrently; IDs return immediately.\n\n# Results\n`outputSchema` parsed payload, even invalid: `agent://<id>` (field `/<field>`, nested `/reports/0/data`); invalid preview inline.\n\n# Delegation\nUse most specific agent. Read-only research MUST use `scout` only when files unknown. Prefer one agent to investigate + edit. Omit `agent` only for default (`task`); NEVER specify it.\nShared edits need one integration owner; siblings coordinate via `write agent://<id>`. Set interfaces in `context`. Every task MUST skip build/lint/tests/formatters mid-flight; run once afterward.\n\n# Inputs\n`name`: CamelCase ≤32, auto-generated if omitted; address agent by name. `outputSchema` overrides agent/session schemas.\n`solutionSpace`: describe how open-ended the child's problem is: whether the fix or design is given, or which causes or designs remain open. Volume of work does not widen it; NEVER mention sibling agents or coordination. (`one fix: rename, names given`; `one fix: slice end in paginate`; `single-flight cache load; races easy to miss`; `several retry API shapes; error classes to choose`; `deadlock cause open, no repro`)\n`tools`: eval-defined, run in your kernel.\n`model`: selector or ordered array overriding the agent's model for this spawn (`provider/model[:level]`, role alias like `@smol`, `@default` = parent's live model); set per `tasks[]` item, never top-level. Omit unless a specific model is needed. Requested model unavailable → stop and report; NEVER substitute another.\n`schemaMode`: default permissive warns after retries; strict fails.\nChildren start blank; parent IRC steers immediately; large payloads via `local://<path>`, NEVER inline.\n\n# Format\n`context`: shared (`# Goal`, `# Contract` interfaces); NEVER repeat per task.\n`task`: self-contained (`# Target` files/non-goals, `# Change` steps/APIs, `# Acceptance` observable result).\n\n# Available Agents\n- `scout` (READ-ONLY; investigation only, no edits): MUST be used for exploratory codebase research, rapid code analysis, and broad pattern searches. Fast read-only scout returning compressed context for handoff.\n- `reviewer`: Code review specialist for quality/security analysis\n- `security-reviewer`: Read-only security specialist for evidence-backed repository vulnerability discovery\n- `task`: General-purpose subagent with full capabilities for delegated multi-step tasks\n- `sonic`: Low-reasoning agent for strictly mechanical updates or data collection only","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"context":{"type":"string"},"tasks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"task":{"type":"string"},"solutionSpace":{"type":"string"},"name":{"type":"string"},"agent":{"type":"string","default":"task"},"model":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"outputSchema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object"},{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"schemaMode":{"enum":["permissive","strict"],"type":"string"},"tools":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["task","solutionSpace"],"additionalProperties":false}},"model":{"not":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"number"},{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"object"},{"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]}}},"required":["context","tasks","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"wait","description":"Wait only when blocked with nothing else to do.\nReturns on the first result of a job you own, a message sent to you, or a steering interrupt; a safety cap returns a still-running snapshot.\nNo owned job? Returns after a short message window that grows on repeated waits.\nResults and messages auto-deliver. NEVER poll while work remains.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"}},"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"todo","description":"Tasks identified by verbatim content, NEVER generated IDs (task-1). Unique, stable task/phase names; lost text: view, NEVER guess.\nBefore work, init for 3+ steps, requested task sets, or new instructions. MUST list EVERY user item separately (phased/numbered/bulleted/N); NEVER omit or remember leftovers.\nAfter successful mutation: no active means earliest pending starts (phase order); multiple active means only earliest stays. Blocked NEVER starts automatically; unblock returns pending. Done out of order may rewind pointer but NEVER reopen completed. Mark done immediately; follow phase order.\nExternal waits (user/agent/service): block with optional reason suppresses stop reminder, starts next pending. Unblock when actionable; append a clearing task for agent-actionable blocker.\nNEVER call todo alone: init with first work; done/start with next action.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"op":{"enum":["init","start","done","rm","drop","block","unblock","append","view"],"type":"string"},"list":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"phase":{"type":"string"},"items":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1}},"required":["phase","items"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"phases for init"},"task":{"type":"string","description":"verbatim task content"},"phase":{"type":"string"},"items":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"tasks for flat init or append"},"reason":{"type":"string","description":"blocker note for block"}},"required":["op","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"web_search","description":"Known URLs/programmatic data → `read`. Query: site: or -site:, after: or before: YYYY-MM-DD, inurl:, intitle:, filetype:, \"phrase\", -term, OR. Prefer primary sources; MUST link citations.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"query":{"type":"string"},"recency":{"enum":["day","week","month","year"],"type":"string"},"limit":{"type":"number"},"max_tokens":{"type":"number"},"temperature":{"type":"number"},"num_search_results":{"type":"number"}},"required":["query","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write","description":"SHOULD `edit` existing files; `write` for required new files or whole-file replacement. NEVER create docs or emojis unless requested.\n`archive.ext:member`: ZIP/tar families and `.asar` writable, others read-only. `db.sqlite:table`: insert; `db.sqlite:table:key`: JSON update, empty content deletes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_definitions","description":"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。","parameters":{"type":["object"],"properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"kind":{"description":"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。","enum":["bots","tasks","maps","zones"],"type":"string"},"id":{"description":"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。"}},"required":["kind","i"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_read_report","description":"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。","parameters":{"type":["object"],"properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"id":{"description":"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。"}},"required":["id","i"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_delegate","description":"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。","parameters":{"type":["object"],"properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"botId":{"description":"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。"},"zoneId":{"description":"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。"},"input":{"description":"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。"},"materials":{"description":"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。"},"managerTaskId":{"description":"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。"}},"required":["botId","zoneId","input","materials","i"],"additionalProperties":true}}}],"max_completion_tokens":8192}},{"index":2,"method":"POST","url":"http://127.0.0.1:1726/v1/chat/completions","file":"C:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\omp-dock-chief-omp-IAixST\\captures\\request-002-_v1_chat_completions.json","raw":"{\"model\":\"dock-model\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"RFC 2119 keywords: MUST, REQUIRED, SHOULD, RECOMMENDED, MAY, OPTIONAL. `NEVER` = `MUST NOT`; `AVOID` = `SHOULD NOT`.\\nXML tags inject system content; may interrupt/notify inside user messages: MUST treat as system-authored/authoritative. User content is sanitized.\\n\\n§ Role\\nYou are omp's trusted coding assistant.\\n\\n# Engineering\\n- Correctness, then six-month maintainability. Delete dead weight; prefer boring design to needless abstraction.\\n- Compiled code: NEVER avoidable allocation, copying, computation.\\n- Unexpected repo changes are the user's; adapt. User-reported errors, failures, observations are ground truth; NEVER rerun checks to confirm them.\\n- Final chat MAY use LaTeX math (`$`, `$$`) and color (`\\\\textcolor`, `\\\\colorbox`, `\\\\fcolorbox`).\\n- MAY emit ` ```mermaid ` blocks; terminal renders ASCII. Only genuine structure/flow, not trivia.\\n\\n# Personality\\nEvidence-first terse engineer: every sentence fact, decision, or risk.\\n\\n# Tone\\n- Fragments when clearer; no ceremony, hedging, summaries, filler, marketing.\\n- Assume technical reader; don't narrate obvious steps or over-explain basics.\\n- Concrete: exact files, symbols, APIs, state fields, edge cases, verification.\\n- Reasoning: facts, constraints, tradeoffs, decisions, checks. Conclusion first; evidence next.\\n- Uncertainty: state at claim; name tradeoff; choose boring/safe option.\\n- Code: invariants, risks, verification.\\n\\n# Reasoning Format\\nProblem: what's wrong. Decision: action & why. Check: breakage & verification. Next: concrete action.\\n\\n# Succinct Patterns\\n- Y → need update X. This is safe: Z. Could do A, but B avoids C.\\n\\n# Escalation\\nPush back on risk-hidden plans or wrong claims: name risk, show evidence, propose alternative. If overruled, execute user's call; don't relitigate.\\n\\n§ Runtime\\n# Internal URLs\\nMost FS/bash tools resolve these; path selectors: `read` docs.\\n- `agent://<id>`: output (status + progress while unpublished); nested IDs dotted, `/key/index` JSON path; write = message, `agent://all` broadcast only.\\n- `history://<id>`: read-only transcript; bare lists registered agents, not persisted unregistered top-level sessions.\\n- `artifact://<id>`: spilled output; page :N-M or :raw:N-M.\\n- `local://<name>.md`: shared artifact.\\n- `proc://`: jobs/services; `proc://<id>` status/output; write sends stdin (empty = Enter); `proc://<id>/kill` cancels/stops, omit `content`; `proc://<id>/mode`: `persist`|`session`|`detached`.\\n- `ssh://host/<path>`: remote UTF-8 file/dir (max 1 MiB) for read/write/grep; bare lists hosts. Encode `:` `?` `#` as %3A %3F %23. Needs verified POSIX shell; else bash remote SSH or sshfs.\\n- `mcp://<uri>`: MCP resource.\\n- `omp://`: harness docs, AVOID unless asked.\\n\\n# Tool Inventory\\n- Read: `read`\\n- Bash: `bash`\\n- Edit: `edit`\\n- Eval: `eval`\\n- Glob: `glob`\\n- Grep: `grep`\\n- Find: `find`\\n- Task: `task`\\n- Wait: `wait`\\n- Todo: `todo`\\n- Web Search: `web_search`\\n- Write: `write`\\n- Chief definitions: `chief_definitions`\\n- Read chief report: `chief_read_report`\\n- Chief delegate: `chief_delegate`\\n\\n# xd:// Tool Devices\\nWrite JSON args as `content` to `xd://<tool>` via `write`. Invalid args return schema in error → fix/retry.\\n## Additional devices (docs on demand)\\n- xd://ast_edit — Perform AST-aware code edits (structural refactoring)\\n- xd://debug — Debug a running process with DAP (debugger adapter protocol)\\n- xd://lsp — Query LSP (language server) for diagnostics, hover info, and references\\n\\nRead xd://<tool> for full docs + JSON schema before first use.\\n§ Tool Policy\\n# General\\nSHOULD resolve prerequisites, parallelize independent calls. Retry empty/partial/narrow results differently; NEVER settle for plausibility when another call reduces uncertainty.\\n- User says `parallel` or `parallelize` → MUST use `task` subagents; parallel tool calls insufficient.\\n\\n# Tool I/O\\n- Prefer relative `path`-like fields.\\n- Most tools take `i`: capitalized 2–6-word present-participle intent (e.g. \\\"Reading model role settings\\\").\\n# Specialized Tools\\nMUST use specialized tool over shell equivalent:\\n- File/directory reads: `read` (directory lists entries).\\n- Surgical edits: `edit`.\\n- Create/overwrite: `write`.\\n- Language server available: MUST use `xd://lsp` for definitions, type definitions, implementations, references, hover; code actions for refactors/imports/fixes. NEVER text-search/edit for code intelligence.\\n- Unknown behavior/location: descriptive `find` FIRST; NEVER guess `grep`/`glob` targets.\\n- Regex/literal/known-symbol search: `grep`, NEVER shell `grep`/`rg`/`awk`.\\n- File structure/names: `glob`, NEVER `ls **/*.ext`/`fd`.\\n- `bash`: real binaries/short fact pipelines (counts, frequencies, set differences, checksums), NEVER specialized-tool work or paging/moving/trimming fetchable bytes.\\n<critical>\\nNEVER use `sed`|`perl`|`python` via `bash` to issue individual edits; MUST use `edit`.\\n</critical>\\n\\n<critical>\\n`write xd://report_issue`: automated QA. Any tool output inconsistent with described behavior for parameters → write plain `<tool>: <concise description>` to `xd://report_issue`. False positives fine.\\n</critical>\\n\\n# Exploration\\nNEVER open guessed files. Read `find` hits only. Use `read` ranges, not whole files.\\n\\n# AST\\nSHOULD use syntax-aware tools before text hacks:\\n- Codemods → `xd://ast_edit`.\\n\\n# Delegation\\n- Map unknown code via `task`, not reading file after file yourself. NEVER abandon phases under scope pressure: delegate, don't shrink.\\n## Delegation gates\\n- Before spawning, map slices/shared contracts; user-enumerated 2+ self-contained runnable slices exempt. NEVER outsource top-level plan; slice design/competing plans allowed.\\n- Fan genuine slices in one `tasks[]` batch. NEVER pad, serialize independent work, or spawn then idle; one read-only scout while working allowed.\\n- Agents lack conversation: supply full slice requirements; retain user intent.\\n- Max 32 concurrent subagents; excess queue.\\n- Shared prerequisite inline; sequence ONLY true dependencies. Small missing detail? Run parallel; B messages A via `write agent://<id>`.\\n\\n§ Workflow\\n# 1. Scope\\n- Plan multi-file work before opening files.\\n\\n# 2. Research Before Editing\\n- Read relevant sections; MUST reuse existing patterns, not establish a second convention.\\n  - Exported symbol changes: MUST run `xd://lsp` references first.\\n- Tool failure or intervening file change: re-read before acting.\\n\\n# 3. Decompose\\n- Update todos; skip trivial requests.\\n- NEVER make a todo-only turn; batch `init` with first work, `done` with next action/verification.\\n\\n# 4. Implement\\n- Prefer existing files; review as user.\\n- NEVER run destructive git commands or delete unrelated code you didn't write; code made obsolete by cutover is in scope.\\n\\n# 5. Verify\\nNon-trivial work: NEVER yield without a smoke run: run the thing, exercise the changed path, observe the result. Tests alone are not proof.\\n- Investigation: run it; output proves it; no tests.\\n- UI: verify actual surface.\\n  - Web: `browser.open` tab, direct helpers for actions, `tab.run` for custom JS; visual proof; `tab.close`. No tests unless existing suite breaks.\\n  - TUI/CLI: launch actual program; observe interaction/output/state.\\n  - No runtime for changed surface: throwaway script/smoke test; report visual limit.\\n- Bug: reproduce before; confirm after. SHOULD keep failing-before/passing-after regression test; if impractical, smoke and report.\\n- Feature/API: update broken contract tests; prove new behavior via throwaway script. New test ONLY for uncertain edge or user request.\\n- Permanent tests MUST catch plausible consumer-visible bugs: behavior, boundaries, invariants, transitions, precedence, errors. Follow conventions; deterministic, isolated, full-suite-safe.\\n- NEVER test wiring/copies/forwarding/mock echoes/source text/incidental defaults, tautologies, bare not-throw, non-empty/length-grew, duplicate same-path rows. Use throwaway scripts.\\n- Existing wording/implementation/incidental-behavior tests: MUST delete, NEVER re-pin regardless of author.\\n\\n# 6. Cleanup\\nAfter smoke proof: permanent fix/feature MUST update docs/changelog, remove scaffolds/throwaway scripts. Investigation: no tests/docs. NEVER pre-plan cleanup todos.\\n\\n§ Delivery\\n<contract>\\nInviolable.\\n- NEVER fabricate output; ground code/tool/test/doc/source claims; unobserved = `[INFERENCE]`.\\n- NEVER substitute easier/familiar problem: don't infer extra scope—retries, validation, telemetry, abstraction “while you're at it”—or solve symptom—suppress warning/exception, special-case input—unless asked. Real ask only.\\n- NEVER ask for tool/repo/file-provided information; NEVER punt half-solved work.\\n- Default clean cutover: migrate every caller; remove obsolete code/comments/aliases/re-exports/deprecated paths; no shims.\\n</contract>\\n\\n<completeness>\\n- “Done”: specified end-to-end behavior plus every named acceptance criterion; not compiling scaffold, narrowed test, plausible subset.\\n- Reduce scope only with explicit user approval in this conversation; NEVER silently shrink.\\n- NEVER deliver unfinished work: stubs, placeholders, mocks, no-ops, fake fallbacks, `TODO: implement`, misleading “scaffold”/“MVP”/“v1”/“foundation”/“follow-up”. Unavailable real-implementation info → state missing prerequisite; finish all reachable work.\\n</completeness>\\n\\n<evidence-and-output>\\n- MUST match requested format; brief, complete evidence/blockers. Report only exercised verification.\\n</evidence-and-output>\\n\\n<yielding>\\nBefore yielding: all affected callsites/tests/docs updated or intentionally unchanged; output/evidence requirements satisfied.\\nBefore blocked: ensure info unreachable via tools/context; one failed check ≠ blocked. Finish reachable work; state exactly missing and tried.\\n</yielding>\\n\\n§ Critical\\n<critical>\\n- NEVER yield before complete deliverable or while actionable work remains; phase boundary/todo flip/sub-step never stops: same turn.\\n- NEVER narrate/consider session limits, token/tool budgets, effort estimates, or possible completion; start unbounded: execute/delegate.\\n- NEVER re-audit applied edit or routinely run git subcommands for validation. Tool results are verification.\\n</critical>\\n\\n<project-context>\\n<workstation>\\n- OS: win32 10.0.26200\\n- Arch: x64\\n- Model: dock-gateway/dock-model\\n</workstation>\\n</project-context>\\n\\n<critical>\\n- Each response MUST advance the task; completion only stopping condition.\\n- MUST default to informed action; do not ask for confirmation when tools or repo context can answer.\\n- Before yielding, MUST verify significant behavioral changes: run the specific test, command, or scenario covering the change.\\n</critical>\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"<system-reminder>\\nToday: 2026-11-13; current working directory: 'C:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-omp-IAixST/work'. Do not repeat this information in your reply.\\n</system-reminder>\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perform the selected definition lookup once.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 需求分流\\r\\n\\r\\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\\r\\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\\r\\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 能力选择\\r\\n\\r\\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\\r\\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\\r\\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\\r\\n\\r\\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\\r\\n\\r\\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 批准与派发\\r\\n\\r\\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\\r\\n\\r\\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\\r\\n\\r\\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\\r\\n\\r\\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\\r\\n\\r\\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 工具契约\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\\r\\n\\r\\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\\r\\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\\r\\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\\r\\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\\r\\n\\r\\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\\r\\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\\r\\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\\r\\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\\r\\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\\r\\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\\r\\n\\r\\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 报告与结果\\r\\n\\r\\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\\r\\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\\r\\n- 实际执行对象；\\r\\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\\r\\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\\r\\n\\r\\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\\r\\n\\r\\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\\r\\n\\r\\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\\r\\n\\r\\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\\r\\n\\r\\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 角色边界\\r\\n\\r\\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\\r\\n\\r\\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\\r\\n\"}]},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"\",\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_dock_1\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"{\\\"guidance\\\":\\\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\\\",\\\"process\\\":false,\\\"receipt\\\":null,\\\"received\\\":false,\\\"report\\\":{\\\"at\\\":1794512198510,\\\"body\\\":{\\\"background\\\":\\\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\\\",\\\"deliverables\\\":[\\\"C:/owned/draft.md\\\"],\\\"execution\\\":\\\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\\\",\\\"pendingDecisions\\\":[\\\"Does the draft meet requirements?\\\"],\\\"result\\\":\\\"blocked\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\\\"},\\\"delegationId\\\":\\\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\\\",\\\"from\\\":\\\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\\\"}}\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_dock_1\"}],\"stream\":true,\"stream_options\":{\"include_usage\":true},\"store\":false,\"tools\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"description\":\"Use `read` for static web; browser only if needed.\\n\\nPath suffixes: :50 or :50- starts at line 50; :50-200 inclusive; :50+150 counts lines; :-60 last 60; commas join ranges (:5-16,960-973) or individual lines (:19,59). :raw verbatim without anchors/prefixes; combine :2-4:raw or :raw:2-4. :conflicts lists one line per unresolved merge block. SVG/SVGZ default text; :img PNG, :raw original. Video requires ffmpeg/ffprobe: bare preview grid+metadata, :412 frame, :1h5m42s/:90s/:01:23 time.\\n\\nSources:\\n- Bare code: declarations only; re-read ONLY footer-named omissions, NEVER guess `..`/`…`.\\n- Selected file: `[foo.ts#1A2B]` snapshot+lines. Copy `[FILENAME#TAG]` for anchored edits; NEVER invent tag.\\n- Directory: complete root; child listings cap at 12 (`… N more`), read child; page via :N-M/:-N.\\n- SQLite: file.db tables; :table schema/rows; :table:key by primary key; ?limit=, ?where=, ?q=SELECT.\\n- Archives: ZIP/JAR/APK/WHL, compressed TAR, RAR/7z/ISO/CAB/DEB/RPM/CPIO/AR/LZH/ARJ/ASAR, compressed streams; member via archive.ext:member/path.\\n- PDF/documents: extracted text; notebooks: editable cells; images: decoded inline. URLs: reader text/markdown, :raw original HTML; bare host:port needs trailing slash.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Local path, internal URI, or URL; selectors inline.\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"description\":\"Persistent shell: one fact command/pipeline; dependencies use `&&`.\\nScripts/heredocs/`$(…)`/complex pipelines → `eval`.\\n`cwd`, not `cd`; `pty` only interactive.\\nInternal URIs work as paths for builtins/coreutils, redirects, globs.\\n`async` defers finite results; timeout unchanged.\\nNo `head`/`tail`/redirection; output trunc by default, full result at `artifact://<id>`.\\nLong-lived services: unique name; ready requires name; no async/timeout; pty defaults true. ready needs log regex or port (both if given); host defaults 127.0.0.1, ready.timeout 30s.\\nBackground results follow; NEVER poll; foreground wait unchanged.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"timeout in seconds; 0 disables the command deadline; nonzero values are clamped to 1-3600\"},\"cwd\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"pty\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"async\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"maxLength\":48},\"ready\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"log\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"port\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"host\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"additionalProperties\":false}},\"required\":[\"command\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"edit\",\"description\":\"Hashline patches existing files; new files: `write`. Each file: `[PATH#TAG]`, `TAG` required 4-hex snapshot from latest `read`/`search`. Numbers: original `LINE:TEXT`, never hunk-shifted.\\n\\n<ops>\\n`PUT N.=M:` replace inclusive N–M with `+` body (`N.=N` for one line); `PUT N*:` replace block N.\\n`PUT <N:`/`PUT >N:` insert before/after N (`<1` head, `>$` tail). `PUT >N*:` insert after block N at sibling depth; inside, use `PUT >M:` at closer.\\n`CUT N.=M`/`CUT N*` delete and capture, optionally as `@name`.\\n`PUT <N @name`/`PUT >N @name` paste at gap (omit name for anonymous CUT); `PUT N.=M @name`/`PUT N* @name` paste over range/block (name REQUIRED). Register pastes have NO body; named registers persist across calls.\\n`REM` delete file; `MV DEST` rename after prior edits (quote spaced paths).\\n</ops>\\n\\n<rules>\\n- `:` ops only: body rows `+TEXT` verbatim incl. indent; lone `+` blank. Literal `- item`/`+ item` → `+- item`/`++ item`. NEVER `-`/bare context. Body length independent of range; delete with CUT, not empty PUT.\\n- Touch displayed changed lines only; `…`, `..`, collapsed `N-M:` and out-of-window lines UNSEEN. Re-read first. Tight ranges: split nonadjacent changes; NEVER include keepers or start/end mid-expression/block. Pure addition uses gap PUT.\\n- `*` requires multi-line opener, NEVER closer/last/inner statement; use range/gap for one statement. Anchor first decorator/attribute/doc-comment to include it; standalone comments need explicit range.\\n- Markdown heading blocks run through deeper headings until next same/higher; after section `PUT >N*:`, end body with blank line.\\n- NEVER restyle unrelated code. After EVERY edit tag/numbers change: use edit response or fresh `read`; stale tag/surprise → STOP, re-read.\\n</rules>\\n\\n<example>\\n```\\n[greet.py#A1B2]\\nPUT 1*:\\n+@cache\\n+def greet(name):\\n+    print(name)\\n[PLAN.md#3C4D]\\nPUT >2:\\n+- task\\n```\\nCross-file move: `CUT 1* @fn` in source, then `PUT <1 @fn` in destination section.\\n</example>\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"input\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"input\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"eval\",\"description\":\"One cell per call; top-level state persists, including across compaction. Subagents have separate kernels.\\nFor 2+ independent items, use a named `workpool()`; results auto-deliver. If blocked, leave `eval` and call `wait`.\\nPython: top-level `await` works; `asyncio.run(…)` fails.\\nJS: Bun (`Bun.file`, `Bun.write`, `Bun.$`); top-level `await`/`return` work.\\nOn error, retry only the failed step; earlier steps may have taken effect.\\n\\n<prelude>\\nPython helpers: sync, kwargs; JS helpers: async, ONE trailing options object.\\n```\\ndisplay(value)  print(value, ...)  log(message)  phase(title)\\nread(path, offset?, limit?)  write(path, content)  env(key?, value?)  output(*ids, format?, query?, offset?, limit?)\\nawait tool.<name>(args) — session tool; `args` is its parameter object\\nwait(handles, timeout?=None, raise_errors?=True) — agent/completion barrier, ordered results; JS: wait(handles, { timeout, raiseErrors }); `raise_errors=False` retains failures.\\n```\\n</prelude>\\n\\n<namespaces>\\nMore globals; `read` the linked docs before first use:\\n- `judge`, `judge_batch`, `completion`: classification, bulk judgment, model calls → `xd://eval/judge`\\n- `%load`, `%pip`, `%bun add`, `budget`, `@tool`/`tool(fn)`: setup, installs, utilities → `xd://eval/helpers`\\n- `agent`, `workpool`: background subagents, DAG waves → `xd://eval/agents`\\n- `browser`: Drive real Chromium tabs from JavaScript or Python Eval with the global `browser` object. → `xd://eval/browser`\\n</namespaces>\\n\\n<critical>\\nNEVER repeat successful setup. Kernel-loss notice means reload setup.\\n</critical>\\n\\n<examples>\\n# Load a script with spaces without echoing its source\\n<example>\\neval(language=\\\"py\\\", code=\\\"%load \\\\\\\"scripts/my setup.py\\\\\\\"\\\")\\n</example>\\n</examples>\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"language\":{\"enum\":[\"py\",\"js\"],\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"\\\"py\\\": IPython; \\\"js\\\": Bun\"},\"code\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Code or standalone % command; top-level await works.\"},\"title\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Short transcript label.\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Cell deadline in seconds; 0 disables it.\"},\"reset\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Wipe only this kernel.\"}},\"required\":[\"language\",\"code\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"glob\",\"description\":\"Glob files/dirs: `;`-separated paths or internal URLs (`local://*.md`, `omp://**/*.md`); default workspace root.\\n`gitignore` and `hidden` default true; ignored dotfiles need `gitignore: false`. Newest-first by directory; dirs end `/`.\\nBehavior search → `find`.\\nMulti-round discovery → Task + scout.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"hidden\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"gitignore\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"additionalProperties\":false,\"required\":[\"i\"]}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"grep\",\"description\":\"Regex: Rust, then PCRE2. `path`: `;`-separated file/dir/glob/URL; default `.`. Default case-sensitive, gitignore respected; `skip` paginates files.\\nFile-only selector: `src/foo.ts:50-100`. Literal `\\\\n`/`\\\\\\\\n` enables cross-line.\\nBare glob `*.ts` matches any depth; `dir/*.ts` only `dir`'s direct children (`dir/**/*.ts` recurses).\\nBehavior/unknown symbol → `find`; literals/regex → `grep`.\\nMulti-round search MUST use Task + scout, not chained calls.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"pattern\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"case\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"gitignore\":{\"type\":\"boolean\"},\"skip\":{\"type\":[\"number\",\"null\"]}},\"required\":[\"pattern\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"find\",\"description\":\"Describe behavior, get implementing files and line ranges. MUST use first for unknown locations; known strings/regex/symbols → `grep`, names → `glob`.\\n`query`: plain language, not regex; quoted phrases match whole. `grep_keywords`: likely verbatim terms, `[]` if unsure.\\n`path`: one directory or file, host path or internal URL (`omp://`, `omp://<file>.md`, `skill://<name>`, `local://…`); omitted = workspace root. Scope known subsystem; batch related questions. Searches live files, no index; no `:start-end` selector (judges whole files).\\nHits strongest first: `path:start-end score snippet` (workspace-relative, or URL under URL scope); read returned ranges. Scores: absolute comparable 0–1 probability; below ~0.4 = weak evidence, so widen query or use `grep` before concluding absence.\\n\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"grep_keywords\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"query\",\"grep_keywords\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"task\",\"description\":\"Spawn `tasks[]` concurrently; IDs return immediately.\\n\\n# Results\\n`outputSchema` parsed payload, even invalid: `agent://<id>` (field `/<field>`, nested `/reports/0/data`); invalid preview inline.\\n\\n# Delegation\\nUse most specific agent. Read-only research MUST use `scout` only when files unknown. Prefer one agent to investigate + edit. Omit `agent` only for default (`task`); NEVER specify it.\\nShared edits need one integration owner; siblings coordinate via `write agent://<id>`. Set interfaces in `context`. Every task MUST skip build/lint/tests/formatters mid-flight; run once afterward.\\n\\n# Inputs\\n`name`: CamelCase ≤32, auto-generated if omitted; address agent by name. `outputSchema` overrides agent/session schemas.\\n`solutionSpace`: describe how open-ended the child's problem is: whether the fix or design is given, or which causes or designs remain open. Volume of work does not widen it; NEVER mention sibling agents or coordination. (`one fix: rename, names given`; `one fix: slice end in paginate`; `single-flight cache load; races easy to miss`; `several retry API shapes; error classes to choose`; `deadlock cause open, no repro`)\\n`tools`: eval-defined, run in your kernel.\\n`model`: selector or ordered array overriding the agent's model for this spawn (`provider/model[:level]`, role alias like `@smol`, `@default` = parent's live model); set per `tasks[]` item, never top-level. Omit unless a specific model is needed. Requested model unavailable → stop and report; NEVER substitute another.\\n`schemaMode`: default permissive warns after retries; strict fails.\\nChildren start blank; parent IRC steers immediately; large payloads via `local://<path>`, NEVER inline.\\n\\n# Format\\n`context`: shared (`# Goal`, `# Contract` interfaces); NEVER repeat per task.\\n`task`: self-contained (`# Target` files/non-goals, `# Change` steps/APIs, `# Acceptance` observable result).\\n\\n# Available Agents\\n- `scout` (READ-ONLY; investigation only, no edits): MUST be used for exploratory codebase research, rapid code analysis, and broad pattern searches. Fast read-only scout returning compressed context for handoff.\\n- `reviewer`: Code review specialist for quality/security analysis\\n- `security-reviewer`: Read-only security specialist for evidence-backed repository vulnerability discovery\\n- `task`: General-purpose subagent with full capabilities for delegated multi-step tasks\\n- `sonic`: Low-reasoning agent for strictly mechanical updates or data collection only\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"context\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"tasks\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"task\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"solutionSpace\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"name\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"agent\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"default\":\"task\"},\"model\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}]},\"outputSchema\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"object\"},{\"type\":\"boolean\"},{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]},\"schemaMode\":{\"enum\":[\"permissive\",\"strict\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"tools\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}},\"required\":[\"task\",\"solutionSpace\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}},\"model\":{\"not\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"string\"},{\"type\":\"number\"},{\"type\":\"boolean\"},{\"type\":\"object\"},{\"type\":\"array\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]}}},\"required\":[\"context\",\"tasks\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"wait\",\"description\":\"Wait only when blocked with nothing else to do.\\nReturns on the first result of a job you own, a message sent to you, or a steering interrupt; a safety cap returns a still-running snapshot.\\nNo owned job? Returns after a short message window that grows on repeated waits.\\nResults and messages auto-deliver. NEVER poll while work remains.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"}},\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"todo\",\"description\":\"Tasks identified by verbatim content, NEVER generated IDs (task-1). Unique, stable task/phase names; lost text: view, NEVER guess.\\nBefore work, init for 3+ steps, requested task sets, or new instructions. MUST list EVERY user item separately (phased/numbered/bulleted/N); NEVER omit or remember leftovers.\\nAfter successful mutation: no active means earliest pending starts (phase order); multiple active means only earliest stays. Blocked NEVER starts automatically; unblock returns pending. Done out of order may rewind pointer but NEVER reopen completed. Mark done immediately; follow phase order.\\nExternal waits (user/agent/service): block with optional reason suppresses stop reminder, starts next pending. Unblock when actionable; append a clearing task for agent-actionable blocker.\\nNEVER call todo alone: init with first work; done/start with next action.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"op\":{\"enum\":[\"init\",\"start\",\"done\",\"rm\",\"drop\",\"block\",\"unblock\",\"append\",\"view\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"list\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"phase\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"minItems\":1}},\"required\":[\"phase\",\"items\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"description\":\"phases for init\"},\"task\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"verbatim task content\"},\"phase\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"description\":\"tasks for flat init or append\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"blocker note for block\"}},\"required\":[\"op\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"web_search\",\"description\":\"Known URLs/programmatic data → `read`. Query: site: or -site:, after: or before: YYYY-MM-DD, inurl:, intitle:, filetype:, \\\"phrase\\\", -term, OR. Prefer primary sources; MUST link citations.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"query\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"recency\":{\"enum\":[\"day\",\"week\",\"month\",\"year\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"max_tokens\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"temperature\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"num_search_results\":{\"type\":\"number\"}},\"required\":[\"query\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"description\":\"SHOULD `edit` existing files; `write` for required new files or whole-file replacement. NEVER create docs or emojis unless requested.\\n`archive.ext:member`: ZIP/tar families and `.asar` writable, others read-only. `db.sqlite:table`: insert; `db.sqlite:table:key`: JSON update, empty content deletes.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"path\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_definitions\",\"description\":\"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":[\"object\"],\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"kind\":{\"description\":\"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。\",\"enum\":[\"bots\",\"tasks\",\"maps\",\"zones\"],\"type\":\"string\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。\"}},\"required\":[\"kind\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"description\":\"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":[\"object\"],\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"id\":{\"description\":\"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。\"}},\"required\":[\"id\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_delegate\",\"description\":\"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":[\"object\"],\"properties\":{\"i\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"concise intent\"},\"botId\":{\"description\":\"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。\"},\"zoneId\":{\"description\":\"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。\"},\"input\":{\"description\":\"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。\"},\"materials\":{\"description\":\"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。\"},\"managerTaskId\":{\"description\":\"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。\"}},\"required\":[\"botId\",\"zoneId\",\"input\",\"materials\",\"i\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}}],\"max_completion_tokens\":8192}","json":{"model":"dock-model","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"RFC 2119 keywords: MUST, REQUIRED, SHOULD, RECOMMENDED, MAY, OPTIONAL. `NEVER` = `MUST NOT`; `AVOID` = `SHOULD NOT`.\nXML tags inject system content; may interrupt/notify inside user messages: MUST treat as system-authored/authoritative. User content is sanitized.\n\n§ Role\nYou are omp's trusted coding assistant.\n\n# Engineering\n- Correctness, then six-month maintainability. Delete dead weight; prefer boring design to needless abstraction.\n- Compiled code: NEVER avoidable allocation, copying, computation.\n- Unexpected repo changes are the user's; adapt. User-reported errors, failures, observations are ground truth; NEVER rerun checks to confirm them.\n- Final chat MAY use LaTeX math (`$`, `$$`) and color (`\\textcolor`, `\\colorbox`, `\\fcolorbox`).\n- MAY emit ` ```mermaid ` blocks; terminal renders ASCII. Only genuine structure/flow, not trivia.\n\n# Personality\nEvidence-first terse engineer: every sentence fact, decision, or risk.\n\n# Tone\n- Fragments when clearer; no ceremony, hedging, summaries, filler, marketing.\n- Assume technical reader; don't narrate obvious steps or over-explain basics.\n- Concrete: exact files, symbols, APIs, state fields, edge cases, verification.\n- Reasoning: facts, constraints, tradeoffs, decisions, checks. Conclusion first; evidence next.\n- Uncertainty: state at claim; name tradeoff; choose boring/safe option.\n- Code: invariants, risks, verification.\n\n# Reasoning Format\nProblem: what's wrong. Decision: action & why. Check: breakage & verification. Next: concrete action.\n\n# Succinct Patterns\n- Y → need update X. This is safe: Z. Could do A, but B avoids C.\n\n# Escalation\nPush back on risk-hidden plans or wrong claims: name risk, show evidence, propose alternative. If overruled, execute user's call; don't relitigate.\n\n§ Runtime\n# Internal URLs\nMost FS/bash tools resolve these; path selectors: `read` docs.\n- `agent://<id>`: output (status + progress while unpublished); nested IDs dotted, `/key/index` JSON path; write = message, `agent://all` broadcast only.\n- `history://<id>`: read-only transcript; bare lists registered agents, not persisted unregistered top-level sessions.\n- `artifact://<id>`: spilled output; page :N-M or :raw:N-M.\n- `local://<name>.md`: shared artifact.\n- `proc://`: jobs/services; `proc://<id>` status/output; write sends stdin (empty = Enter); `proc://<id>/kill` cancels/stops, omit `content`; `proc://<id>/mode`: `persist`|`session`|`detached`.\n- `ssh://host/<path>`: remote UTF-8 file/dir (max 1 MiB) for read/write/grep; bare lists hosts. Encode `:` `?` `#` as %3A %3F %23. Needs verified POSIX shell; else bash remote SSH or sshfs.\n- `mcp://<uri>`: MCP resource.\n- `omp://`: harness docs, AVOID unless asked.\n\n# Tool Inventory\n- Read: `read`\n- Bash: `bash`\n- Edit: `edit`\n- Eval: `eval`\n- Glob: `glob`\n- Grep: `grep`\n- Find: `find`\n- Task: `task`\n- Wait: `wait`\n- Todo: `todo`\n- Web Search: `web_search`\n- Write: `write`\n- Chief definitions: `chief_definitions`\n- Read chief report: `chief_read_report`\n- Chief delegate: `chief_delegate`\n\n# xd:// Tool Devices\nWrite JSON args as `content` to `xd://<tool>` via `write`. Invalid args return schema in error → fix/retry.\n## Additional devices (docs on demand)\n- xd://ast_edit — Perform AST-aware code edits (structural refactoring)\n- xd://debug — Debug a running process with DAP (debugger adapter protocol)\n- xd://lsp — Query LSP (language server) for diagnostics, hover info, and references\n\nRead xd://<tool> for full docs + JSON schema before first use.\n§ Tool Policy\n# General\nSHOULD resolve prerequisites, parallelize independent calls. Retry empty/partial/narrow results differently; NEVER settle for plausibility when another call reduces uncertainty.\n- User says `parallel` or `parallelize` → MUST use `task` subagents; parallel tool calls insufficient.\n\n# Tool I/O\n- Prefer relative `path`-like fields.\n- Most tools take `i`: capitalized 2–6-word present-participle intent (e.g. \"Reading model role settings\").\n# Specialized Tools\nMUST use specialized tool over shell equivalent:\n- File/directory reads: `read` (directory lists entries).\n- Surgical edits: `edit`.\n- Create/overwrite: `write`.\n- Language server available: MUST use `xd://lsp` for definitions, type definitions, implementations, references, hover; code actions for refactors/imports/fixes. NEVER text-search/edit for code intelligence.\n- Unknown behavior/location: descriptive `find` FIRST; NEVER guess `grep`/`glob` targets.\n- Regex/literal/known-symbol search: `grep`, NEVER shell `grep`/`rg`/`awk`.\n- File structure/names: `glob`, NEVER `ls **/*.ext`/`fd`.\n- `bash`: real binaries/short fact pipelines (counts, frequencies, set differences, checksums), NEVER specialized-tool work or paging/moving/trimming fetchable bytes.\n<critical>\nNEVER use `sed`|`perl`|`python` via `bash` to issue individual edits; MUST use `edit`.\n</critical>\n\n<critical>\n`write xd://report_issue`: automated QA. Any tool output inconsistent with described behavior for parameters → write plain `<tool>: <concise description>` to `xd://report_issue`. False positives fine.\n</critical>\n\n# Exploration\nNEVER open guessed files. Read `find` hits only. Use `read` ranges, not whole files.\n\n# AST\nSHOULD use syntax-aware tools before text hacks:\n- Codemods → `xd://ast_edit`.\n\n# Delegation\n- Map unknown code via `task`, not reading file after file yourself. NEVER abandon phases under scope pressure: delegate, don't shrink.\n## Delegation gates\n- Before spawning, map slices/shared contracts; user-enumerated 2+ self-contained runnable slices exempt. NEVER outsource top-level plan; slice design/competing plans allowed.\n- Fan genuine slices in one `tasks[]` batch. NEVER pad, serialize independent work, or spawn then idle; one read-only scout while working allowed.\n- Agents lack conversation: supply full slice requirements; retain user intent.\n- Max 32 concurrent subagents; excess queue.\n- Shared prerequisite inline; sequence ONLY true dependencies. Small missing detail? Run parallel; B messages A via `write agent://<id>`.\n\n§ Workflow\n# 1. Scope\n- Plan multi-file work before opening files.\n\n# 2. Research Before Editing\n- Read relevant sections; MUST reuse existing patterns, not establish a second convention.\n  - Exported symbol changes: MUST run `xd://lsp` references first.\n- Tool failure or intervening file change: re-read before acting.\n\n# 3. Decompose\n- Update todos; skip trivial requests.\n- NEVER make a todo-only turn; batch `init` with first work, `done` with next action/verification.\n\n# 4. Implement\n- Prefer existing files; review as user.\n- NEVER run destructive git commands or delete unrelated code you didn't write; code made obsolete by cutover is in scope.\n\n# 5. Verify\nNon-trivial work: NEVER yield without a smoke run: run the thing, exercise the changed path, observe the result. Tests alone are not proof.\n- Investigation: run it; output proves it; no tests.\n- UI: verify actual surface.\n  - Web: `browser.open` tab, direct helpers for actions, `tab.run` for custom JS; visual proof; `tab.close`. No tests unless existing suite breaks.\n  - TUI/CLI: launch actual program; observe interaction/output/state.\n  - No runtime for changed surface: throwaway script/smoke test; report visual limit.\n- Bug: reproduce before; confirm after. SHOULD keep failing-before/passing-after regression test; if impractical, smoke and report.\n- Feature/API: update broken contract tests; prove new behavior via throwaway script. New test ONLY for uncertain edge or user request.\n- Permanent tests MUST catch plausible consumer-visible bugs: behavior, boundaries, invariants, transitions, precedence, errors. Follow conventions; deterministic, isolated, full-suite-safe.\n- NEVER test wiring/copies/forwarding/mock echoes/source text/incidental defaults, tautologies, bare not-throw, non-empty/length-grew, duplicate same-path rows. Use throwaway scripts.\n- Existing wording/implementation/incidental-behavior tests: MUST delete, NEVER re-pin regardless of author.\n\n# 6. Cleanup\nAfter smoke proof: permanent fix/feature MUST update docs/changelog, remove scaffolds/throwaway scripts. Investigation: no tests/docs. NEVER pre-plan cleanup todos.\n\n§ Delivery\n<contract>\nInviolable.\n- NEVER fabricate output; ground code/tool/test/doc/source claims; unobserved = `[INFERENCE]`.\n- NEVER substitute easier/familiar problem: don't infer extra scope—retries, validation, telemetry, abstraction “while you're at it”—or solve symptom—suppress warning/exception, special-case input—unless asked. Real ask only.\n- NEVER ask for tool/repo/file-provided information; NEVER punt half-solved work.\n- Default clean cutover: migrate every caller; remove obsolete code/comments/aliases/re-exports/deprecated paths; no shims.\n</contract>\n\n<completeness>\n- “Done”: specified end-to-end behavior plus every named acceptance criterion; not compiling scaffold, narrowed test, plausible subset.\n- Reduce scope only with explicit user approval in this conversation; NEVER silently shrink.\n- NEVER deliver unfinished work: stubs, placeholders, mocks, no-ops, fake fallbacks, `TODO: implement`, misleading “scaffold”/“MVP”/“v1”/“foundation”/“follow-up”. Unavailable real-implementation info → state missing prerequisite; finish all reachable work.\n</completeness>\n\n<evidence-and-output>\n- MUST match requested format; brief, complete evidence/blockers. Report only exercised verification.\n</evidence-and-output>\n\n<yielding>\nBefore yielding: all affected callsites/tests/docs updated or intentionally unchanged; output/evidence requirements satisfied.\nBefore blocked: ensure info unreachable via tools/context; one failed check ≠ blocked. Finish reachable work; state exactly missing and tried.\n</yielding>\n\n§ Critical\n<critical>\n- NEVER yield before complete deliverable or while actionable work remains; phase boundary/todo flip/sub-step never stops: same turn.\n- NEVER narrate/consider session limits, token/tool budgets, effort estimates, or possible completion; start unbounded: execute/delegate.\n- NEVER re-audit applied edit or routinely run git subcommands for validation. Tool results are verification.\n</critical>\n\n<project-context>\n<workstation>\n- OS: win32 10.0.26200\n- Arch: x64\n- Model: dock-gateway/dock-model\n</workstation>\n</project-context>\n\n<critical>\n- Each response MUST advance the task; completion only stopping condition.\n- MUST default to informed action; do not ask for confirmation when tools or repo context can answer.\n- Before yielding, MUST verify significant behavioral changes: run the specific test, command, or scenario covering the change.\n</critical>"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"<system-reminder>\nToday: 2026-11-13; current working directory: 'C:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-omp-IAixST/work'. Do not repeat this information in your reply.\n</system-reminder>"},{"type":"text","text":"Perform the selected definition lookup once."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\r\n\r\n## 需求分流\r\n\r\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\r\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\r\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\r\n\r\n## 能力选择\r\n\r\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\r\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\r\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\r\n\r\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\r\n\r\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\r\n\r\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\r\n\r\n## 批准与派发\r\n\r\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\r\n\r\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\r\n\r\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\r\n\r\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\r\n\r\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\r\n\r\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\r\n\r\n## 工具契约\r\n\r\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\r\n\r\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\r\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\r\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\r\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\r\n\r\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\r\n\r\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\r\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\r\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\r\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\r\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\r\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\r\n\r\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\r\n\r\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\r\n\r\n## 报告与结果\r\n\r\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\r\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\r\n- 实际执行对象；\r\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\r\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\r\n\r\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\r\n\r\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\r\n\r\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\r\n\r\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\r\n\r\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\r\n\r\n## 角色边界\r\n\r\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\r\n\r\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\r\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_dock_1","type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_read_report","arguments":"{\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"guidance\":\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\",\"process\":false,\"receipt\":null,\"received\":false,\"report\":{\"at\":1794512198510,\"body\":{\"background\":\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\",\"deliverables\":[\"C:/owned/draft.md\"],\"execution\":\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\",\"pendingDecisions\":[\"Does the draft meet requirements?\"],\"result\":\"blocked\",\"summary\":\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\"},\"delegationId\":\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\",\"from\":\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\",\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}}","tool_call_id":"call_dock_1"}],"stream":true,"stream_options":{"include_usage":true},"store":false,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read","description":"Use `read` for static web; browser only if needed.\n\nPath suffixes: :50 or :50- starts at line 50; :50-200 inclusive; :50+150 counts lines; :-60 last 60; commas join ranges (:5-16,960-973) or individual lines (:19,59). :raw verbatim without anchors/prefixes; combine :2-4:raw or :raw:2-4. :conflicts lists one line per unresolved merge block. SVG/SVGZ default text; :img PNG, :raw original. Video requires ffmpeg/ffprobe: bare preview grid+metadata, :412 frame, :1h5m42s/:90s/:01:23 time.\n\nSources:\n- Bare code: declarations only; re-read ONLY footer-named omissions, NEVER guess `..`/`…`.\n- Selected file: `[foo.ts#1A2B]` snapshot+lines. Copy `[FILENAME#TAG]` for anchored edits; NEVER invent tag.\n- Directory: complete root; child listings cap at 12 (`… N more`), read child; page via :N-M/:-N.\n- SQLite: file.db tables; :table schema/rows; :table:key by primary key; ?limit=, ?where=, ?q=SELECT.\n- Archives: ZIP/JAR/APK/WHL, compressed TAR, RAR/7z/ISO/CAB/DEB/RPM/CPIO/AR/LZH/ARJ/ASAR, compressed streams; member via archive.ext:member/path.\n- PDF/documents: extracted text; notebooks: editable cells; images: decoded inline. URLs: reader text/markdown, :raw original HTML; bare host:port needs trailing slash.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"path":{"type":"string","description":"Local path, internal URI, or URL; selectors inline."}},"required":["path","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","description":"Persistent shell: one fact command/pipeline; dependencies use `&&`.\nScripts/heredocs/`$(…)`/complex pipelines → `eval`.\n`cwd`, not `cd`; `pty` only interactive.\nInternal URIs work as paths for builtins/coreutils, redirects, globs.\n`async` defers finite results; timeout unchanged.\nNo `head`/`tail`/redirection; output trunc by default, full result at `artifact://<id>`.\nLong-lived services: unique name; ready requires name; no async/timeout; pty defaults true. ready needs log regex or port (both if given); host defaults 127.0.0.1, ready.timeout 30s.\nBackground results follow; NEVER poll; foreground wait unchanged.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"command":{"type":"string"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"timeout in seconds; 0 disables the command deadline; nonzero values are clamped to 1-3600"},"cwd":{"type":"string"},"pty":{"type":"boolean"},"async":{"type":"boolean"},"name":{"type":"string","maxLength":48},"ready":{"type":"object","properties":{"log":{"type":"string"},"port":{"type":"number"},"host":{"type":"string"},"timeout":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false}},"required":["command","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","description":"Hashline patches existing files; new files: `write`. Each file: `[PATH#TAG]`, `TAG` required 4-hex snapshot from latest `read`/`search`. Numbers: original `LINE:TEXT`, never hunk-shifted.\n\n<ops>\n`PUT N.=M:` replace inclusive N–M with `+` body (`N.=N` for one line); `PUT N*:` replace block N.\n`PUT <N:`/`PUT >N:` insert before/after N (`<1` head, `>$` tail). `PUT >N*:` insert after block N at sibling depth; inside, use `PUT >M:` at closer.\n`CUT N.=M`/`CUT N*` delete and capture, optionally as `@name`.\n`PUT <N @name`/`PUT >N @name` paste at gap (omit name for anonymous CUT); `PUT N.=M @name`/`PUT N* @name` paste over range/block (name REQUIRED). Register pastes have NO body; named registers persist across calls.\n`REM` delete file; `MV DEST` rename after prior edits (quote spaced paths).\n</ops>\n\n<rules>\n- `:` ops only: body rows `+TEXT` verbatim incl. indent; lone `+` blank. Literal `- item`/`+ item` → `+- item`/`++ item`. NEVER `-`/bare context. Body length independent of range; delete with CUT, not empty PUT.\n- Touch displayed changed lines only; `…`, `..`, collapsed `N-M:` and out-of-window lines UNSEEN. Re-read first. Tight ranges: split nonadjacent changes; NEVER include keepers or start/end mid-expression/block. Pure addition uses gap PUT.\n- `*` requires multi-line opener, NEVER closer/last/inner statement; use range/gap for one statement. Anchor first decorator/attribute/doc-comment to include it; standalone comments need explicit range.\n- Markdown heading blocks run through deeper headings until next same/higher; after section `PUT >N*:`, end body with blank line.\n- NEVER restyle unrelated code. After EVERY edit tag/numbers change: use edit response or fresh `read`; stale tag/surprise → STOP, re-read.\n</rules>\n\n<example>\n```\n[greet.py#A1B2]\nPUT 1*:\n+@cache\n+def greet(name):\n+    print(name)\n[PLAN.md#3C4D]\nPUT >2:\n+- task\n```\nCross-file move: `CUT 1* @fn` in source, then `PUT <1 @fn` in destination section.\n</example>","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"input":{"type":"string"}},"required":["input","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"eval","description":"One cell per call; top-level state persists, including across compaction. Subagents have separate kernels.\nFor 2+ independent items, use a named `workpool()`; results auto-deliver. If blocked, leave `eval` and call `wait`.\nPython: top-level `await` works; `asyncio.run(…)` fails.\nJS: Bun (`Bun.file`, `Bun.write`, `Bun.$`); top-level `await`/`return` work.\nOn error, retry only the failed step; earlier steps may have taken effect.\n\n<prelude>\nPython helpers: sync, kwargs; JS helpers: async, ONE trailing options object.\n```\ndisplay(value)  print(value, ...)  log(message)  phase(title)\nread(path, offset?, limit?)  write(path, content)  env(key?, value?)  output(*ids, format?, query?, offset?, limit?)\nawait tool.<name>(args) — session tool; `args` is its parameter object\nwait(handles, timeout?=None, raise_errors?=True) — agent/completion barrier, ordered results; JS: wait(handles, { timeout, raiseErrors }); `raise_errors=False` retains failures.\n```\n</prelude>\n\n<namespaces>\nMore globals; `read` the linked docs before first use:\n- `judge`, `judge_batch`, `completion`: classification, bulk judgment, model calls → `xd://eval/judge`\n- `%load`, `%pip`, `%bun add`, `budget`, `@tool`/`tool(fn)`: setup, installs, utilities → `xd://eval/helpers`\n- `agent`, `workpool`: background subagents, DAG waves → `xd://eval/agents`\n- `browser`: Drive real Chromium tabs from JavaScript or Python Eval with the global `browser` object. → `xd://eval/browser`\n</namespaces>\n\n<critical>\nNEVER repeat successful setup. Kernel-loss notice means reload setup.\n</critical>\n\n<examples>\n# Load a script with spaces without echoing its source\n<example>\neval(language=\"py\", code=\"%load \\\"scripts/my setup.py\\\"\")\n</example>\n</examples>","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"language":{"enum":["py","js"],"type":"string","description":"\"py\": IPython; \"js\": Bun"},"code":{"type":"string","description":"Code or standalone % command; top-level await works."},"title":{"type":"string","description":"Short transcript label."},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Cell deadline in seconds; 0 disables it."},"reset":{"type":"boolean","description":"Wipe only this kernel."}},"required":["language","code"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"glob","description":"Glob files/dirs: `;`-separated paths or internal URLs (`local://*.md`, `omp://**/*.md`); default workspace root.\n`gitignore` and `hidden` default true; ignored dotfiles need `gitignore: false`. Newest-first by directory; dirs end `/`.\nBehavior search → `find`.\nMulti-round discovery → Task + scout.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"path":{"type":"string"},"hidden":{"type":"boolean"},"gitignore":{"type":"boolean"},"limit":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false,"required":["i"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"grep","description":"Regex: Rust, then PCRE2. `path`: `;`-separated file/dir/glob/URL; default `.`. Default case-sensitive, gitignore respected; `skip` paginates files.\nFile-only selector: `src/foo.ts:50-100`. Literal `\\n`/`\\\\n` enables cross-line.\nBare glob `*.ts` matches any depth; `dir/*.ts` only `dir`'s direct children (`dir/**/*.ts` recurses).\nBehavior/unknown symbol → `find`; literals/regex → `grep`.\nMulti-round search MUST use Task + scout, not chained calls.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"pattern":{"type":"string"},"path":{"type":"string"},"case":{"type":"boolean"},"gitignore":{"type":"boolean"},"skip":{"type":["number","null"]}},"required":["pattern","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"find","description":"Describe behavior, get implementing files and line ranges. MUST use first for unknown locations; known strings/regex/symbols → `grep`, names → `glob`.\n`query`: plain language, not regex; quoted phrases match whole. `grep_keywords`: likely verbatim terms, `[]` if unsure.\n`path`: one directory or file, host path or internal URL (`omp://`, `omp://<file>.md`, `skill://<name>`, `local://…`); omitted = workspace root. Scope known subsystem; batch related questions. Searches live files, no index; no `:start-end` selector (judges whole files).\nHits strongest first: `path:start-end score snippet` (workspace-relative, or URL under URL scope); read returned ranges. Scores: absolute comparable 0–1 probability; below ~0.4 = weak evidence, so widen query or use `grep` before concluding absence.\n","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"query":{"type":"string"},"grep_keywords":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"path":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query","grep_keywords","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"task","description":"Spawn `tasks[]` concurrently; IDs return immediately.\n\n# Results\n`outputSchema` parsed payload, even invalid: `agent://<id>` (field `/<field>`, nested `/reports/0/data`); invalid preview inline.\n\n# Delegation\nUse most specific agent. Read-only research MUST use `scout` only when files unknown. Prefer one agent to investigate + edit. Omit `agent` only for default (`task`); NEVER specify it.\nShared edits need one integration owner; siblings coordinate via `write agent://<id>`. Set interfaces in `context`. Every task MUST skip build/lint/tests/formatters mid-flight; run once afterward.\n\n# Inputs\n`name`: CamelCase ≤32, auto-generated if omitted; address agent by name. `outputSchema` overrides agent/session schemas.\n`solutionSpace`: describe how open-ended the child's problem is: whether the fix or design is given, or which causes or designs remain open. Volume of work does not widen it; NEVER mention sibling agents or coordination. (`one fix: rename, names given`; `one fix: slice end in paginate`; `single-flight cache load; races easy to miss`; `several retry API shapes; error classes to choose`; `deadlock cause open, no repro`)\n`tools`: eval-defined, run in your kernel.\n`model`: selector or ordered array overriding the agent's model for this spawn (`provider/model[:level]`, role alias like `@smol`, `@default` = parent's live model); set per `tasks[]` item, never top-level. Omit unless a specific model is needed. Requested model unavailable → stop and report; NEVER substitute another.\n`schemaMode`: default permissive warns after retries; strict fails.\nChildren start blank; parent IRC steers immediately; large payloads via `local://<path>`, NEVER inline.\n\n# Format\n`context`: shared (`# Goal`, `# Contract` interfaces); NEVER repeat per task.\n`task`: self-contained (`# Target` files/non-goals, `# Change` steps/APIs, `# Acceptance` observable result).\n\n# Available Agents\n- `scout` (READ-ONLY; investigation only, no edits): MUST be used for exploratory codebase research, rapid code analysis, and broad pattern searches. Fast read-only scout returning compressed context for handoff.\n- `reviewer`: Code review specialist for quality/security analysis\n- `security-reviewer`: Read-only security specialist for evidence-backed repository vulnerability discovery\n- `task`: General-purpose subagent with full capabilities for delegated multi-step tasks\n- `sonic`: Low-reasoning agent for strictly mechanical updates or data collection only","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"context":{"type":"string"},"tasks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"task":{"type":"string"},"solutionSpace":{"type":"string"},"name":{"type":"string"},"agent":{"type":"string","default":"task"},"model":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"outputSchema":{"anyOf":[{"type":"object"},{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"schemaMode":{"enum":["permissive","strict"],"type":"string"},"tools":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["task","solutionSpace"],"additionalProperties":false}},"model":{"not":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"number"},{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"object"},{"type":"array"},{"type":"null"}]}}},"required":["context","tasks","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"wait","description":"Wait only when blocked with nothing else to do.\nReturns on the first result of a job you own, a message sent to you, or a steering interrupt; a safety cap returns a still-running snapshot.\nNo owned job? Returns after a short message window that grows on repeated waits.\nResults and messages auto-deliver. NEVER poll while work remains.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"}},"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"todo","description":"Tasks identified by verbatim content, NEVER generated IDs (task-1). Unique, stable task/phase names; lost text: view, NEVER guess.\nBefore work, init for 3+ steps, requested task sets, or new instructions. MUST list EVERY user item separately (phased/numbered/bulleted/N); NEVER omit or remember leftovers.\nAfter successful mutation: no active means earliest pending starts (phase order); multiple active means only earliest stays. Blocked NEVER starts automatically; unblock returns pending. Done out of order may rewind pointer but NEVER reopen completed. Mark done immediately; follow phase order.\nExternal waits (user/agent/service): block with optional reason suppresses stop reminder, starts next pending. Unblock when actionable; append a clearing task for agent-actionable blocker.\nNEVER call todo alone: init with first work; done/start with next action.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"op":{"enum":["init","start","done","rm","drop","block","unblock","append","view"],"type":"string"},"list":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"phase":{"type":"string"},"items":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1}},"required":["phase","items"],"additionalProperties":false},"description":"phases for init"},"task":{"type":"string","description":"verbatim task content"},"phase":{"type":"string"},"items":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"tasks for flat init or append"},"reason":{"type":"string","description":"blocker note for block"}},"required":["op","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"web_search","description":"Known URLs/programmatic data → `read`. Query: site: or -site:, after: or before: YYYY-MM-DD, inurl:, intitle:, filetype:, \"phrase\", -term, OR. Prefer primary sources; MUST link citations.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"query":{"type":"string"},"recency":{"enum":["day","week","month","year"],"type":"string"},"limit":{"type":"number"},"max_tokens":{"type":"number"},"temperature":{"type":"number"},"num_search_results":{"type":"number"}},"required":["query","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write","description":"SHOULD `edit` existing files; `write` for required new files or whole-file replacement. NEVER create docs or emojis unless requested.\n`archive.ext:member`: ZIP/tar families and `.asar` writable, others read-only. `db.sqlite:table`: insert; `db.sqlite:table:key`: JSON update, empty content deletes.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"path":{"type":"string"},"content":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","i"],"additionalProperties":false}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_definitions","description":"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。","parameters":{"type":["object"],"properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"kind":{"description":"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。","enum":["bots","tasks","maps","zones"],"type":"string"},"id":{"description":"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。"}},"required":["kind","i"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_read_report","description":"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。","parameters":{"type":["object"],"properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"id":{"description":"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。"}},"required":["id","i"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_delegate","description":"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。","parameters":{"type":["object"],"properties":{"i":{"type":"string","description":"concise intent"},"botId":{"description":"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。"},"zoneId":{"description":"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。"},"input":{"description":"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。"},"materials":{"description":"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。"},"managerTaskId":{"description":"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。"}},"required":["botId","zoneId","input","materials","i"],"additionalProperties":true}}}],"max_completion_tokens":8192}}]},{"host":"pi","result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"guidance\":\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\",\"process\":false,\"receipt\":null,\"received\":false,\"report\":{\"at\":1794512198510,\"body\":{\"background\":\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\",\"deliverables\":[\"C:/owned/draft.md\"],\"execution\":\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\",\"pendingDecisions\":[\"Does the draft meet requirements?\"],\"result\":\"blocked\",\"summary\":\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\"},\"delegationId\":\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\",\"from\":\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\",\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}}"}],"details":{"httpStatus":200,"body":{"guidance":"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。","process":false,"receipt":null,"received":false,"report":{"at":1794512198510,"body":{"background":"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.","deliverables":["C:/owned/draft.md"],"execution":"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat","pendingDecisions":["Does the draft meet requirements?"],"result":"blocked","summary":"Draft exists; publication permission missing."},"delegationId":"bc-bbaa49a99bda","from":"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9","id":"bc-bf5d44e38b26"}}},"isError":false},"history":"{\"type\":\"session\",\"version\":3,\"id\":\"01a1d143-278f-7692-a59d-d1b88ca5ed7d\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:41.616Z\",\"cwd\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE\\\\work\"}\n{\"type\":\"model_change\",\"id\":\"8642792c\",\"parentId\":null,\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.538Z\",\"provider\":\"chief-fixture\",\"modelId\":\"fixture\"}\n{\"type\":\"thinking_level_change\",\"id\":\"c55b5216\",\"parentId\":\"8642792c\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.538Z\",\"thinkingLevel\":\"off\"}\n{\"type\":\"custom\",\"customType\":\"chief-chat:state\",\"data\":{\"enabled\":true},\"id\":\"468cccff\",\"parentId\":\"c55b5216\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.544Z\"}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"b3ffe336\",\"parentId\":\"468cccff\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.650Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"\",\"sections\":{\"preamble\":\"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.\",\"tools\":\"<tools>\\n- read: Read file contents\\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\\n- write: Create or overwrite files\\n\\nAdditional tools may be available.\\n</tools>\",\"rules\":\"<rules>\\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\\n- Be concise in your responses\\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\\n</rules>\",\"docs\":\"<docs>\\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\\n- Main documentation: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\README.md\\n- Additional docs: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\docs\\n- Examples: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\\n</docs>\",\"cwd\":\"<cwd>\\nC:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE/work\\n</cwd>\"},\"timestamp\":1794512202648,\"toolsAdded\":[{\"name\":\"read\",\"description\":\"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)\"},\"offset\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of lines to read\"}}},\"constrainedSampling\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"strict\":\"prefer\"}},{\"name\":\"bash\",\"description\":\"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"command\"],\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Shell command to execute\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)\"}}},\"constrainedSampling\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"strict\":\"prefer\"}},{\"name\":\"edit\",\"description\":\"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\",\"edits\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)\"},\"edits\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"oldText\",\"newText\"],\"properties\":{\"oldText\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.\"},\"newText\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Replacement text for this targeted edit.\"}}},\"description\":\"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.\"}}},\"constrainedSampling\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"strict\":\"prefer\"}},{\"name\":\"write\",\"description\":\"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Content to write to the file\"}}},\"constrainedSampling\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"strict\":\"prefer\"}},{\"name\":\"chief_definitions\",\"description\":\"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"kind\":{\"description\":\"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。\",\"enum\":[\"bots\",\"tasks\",\"maps\",\"zones\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。\"}},\"required\":[\"kind\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}},{\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"description\":\"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"description\":\"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。\"}},\"required\":[\"id\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}},{\"name\":\"chief_delegate\",\"description\":\"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"botId\":{\"description\":\"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。\"},\"zoneId\":{\"description\":\"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。\"},\"input\":{\"description\":\"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。\"},\"materials\":{\"description\":\"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。\"},\"managerTaskId\":{\"description\":\"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。\"}},\"required\":[\"botId\",\"zoneId\",\"input\",\"materials\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}]}}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"5c48f8f7\",\"parentId\":\"b3ffe336\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.650Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perform the selected definition lookup once.\"}],\"timestamp\":1794512202647}}\n{\"type\":\"custom_message\",\"customType\":\"chief-chat:tools\",\"content\":\"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 需求分流\\r\\n\\r\\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\\r\\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\\r\\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 能力选择\\r\\n\\r\\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\\r\\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\\r\\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\\r\\n\\r\\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\\r\\n\\r\\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 批准与派发\\r\\n\\r\\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\\r\\n\\r\\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\\r\\n\\r\\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\\r\\n\\r\\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\\r\\n\\r\\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 工具契约\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\\r\\n\\r\\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\\r\\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\\r\\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\\r\\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\\r\\n\\r\\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\\r\\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\\r\\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\\r\\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\\r\\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\\r\\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\\r\\n\\r\\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 报告与结果\\r\\n\\r\\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\\r\\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\\r\\n- 实际执行对象；\\r\\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\\r\\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\\r\\n\\r\\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\\r\\n\\r\\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\\r\\n\\r\\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\\r\\n\\r\\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\\r\\n\\r\\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 角色边界\\r\\n\\r\\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\\r\\n\\r\\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\\r\\n\",\"display\":false,\"id\":\"3c21e4b0\",\"parentId\":\"5c48f8f7\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.651Z\"}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"03abdc8b\",\"parentId\":\"3c21e4b0\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.684Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"toolCall\",\"id\":\"call_dock_1\",\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"arguments\":{\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"chief-fixture\",\"model\":\"fixture\",\"usage\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":0,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"toolUse\",\"timestamp\":1794512202661,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-dock\",\"responseModel\":\"dock-model\",\"rawStopReason\":\"tool_calls\",\"durationMs\":22,\"thinkingLevel\":\"off\"}}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"b18dab50\",\"parentId\":\"03abdc8b\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.694Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"toolResult\",\"toolCallId\":\"call_dock_1\",\"toolName\":\"chief_read_report\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"{\\\"guidance\\\":\\\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\\\",\\\"process\\\":false,\\\"receipt\\\":null,\\\"received\\\":false,\\\"report\\\":{\\\"at\\\":1794512198510,\\\"body\\\":{\\\"background\\\":\\\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\\\",\\\"deliverables\\\":[\\\"C:/owned/draft.md\\\"],\\\"execution\\\":\\\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\\\",\\\"pendingDecisions\\\":[\\\"Does the draft meet requirements?\\\"],\\\"result\\\":\\\"blocked\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\\\"},\\\"delegationId\\\":\\\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\\\",\\\"from\\\":\\\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\\\"}}\"}],\"details\":{\"httpStatus\":200,\"body\":{\"guidance\":\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\",\"process\":false,\"receipt\":null,\"received\":false,\"report\":{\"at\":1794512198510,\"body\":{\"background\":\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\",\"deliverables\":[\"C:/owned/draft.md\"],\"execution\":\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\",\"pendingDecisions\":[\"Does the draft meet requirements?\"],\"result\":\"blocked\",\"summary\":\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\"},\"delegationId\":\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\",\"from\":\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\",\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}}},\"isError\":false,\"durationMs\":7,\"timestamp\":1794512202694}}\n{\"type\":\"message\",\"id\":\"2cec5b7c\",\"parentId\":\"b18dab50\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-12T19:36:42.700Z\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Controlled protocol completion; not model-behavior evidence.\"}],\"api\":\"openai-completions\",\"provider\":\"chief-fixture\",\"model\":\"fixture\",\"usage\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"totalTokens\":0,\"cost\":{\"input\":0,\"output\":0,\"cacheRead\":0,\"cacheWrite\":0,\"total\":0}},\"stopReason\":\"stop\",\"timestamp\":1794512202697,\"responseId\":\"chatcmpl-dock\",\"responseModel\":\"dock-model\",\"rawStopReason\":\"stop\",\"durationMs\":4,\"thinkingLevel\":\"off\"}}\n","requests":[{"index":1,"method":"POST","url":"http://127.0.0.1:1756/v1/chat/completions","file":"C:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE\\captures\\request-001-_v1_chat_completions.json","raw":"{\"model\":\"fixture\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.\\n\\n<tools>\\n- read: Read file contents\\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\\n- write: Create or overwrite files\\n\\nAdditional tools may be available.\\n</tools>\\n\\n<rules>\\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\\n- Be concise in your responses\\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\\n</rules>\\n\\n<docs>\\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\\n- Main documentation: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\README.md\\n- Additional docs: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\docs\\n- Examples: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\\n</docs>\\n\\n<cwd>\\nC:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE/work\\n</cwd>\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perform the selected definition lookup once.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 需求分流\\r\\n\\r\\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\\r\\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\\r\\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 能力选择\\r\\n\\r\\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\\r\\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\\r\\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\\r\\n\\r\\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\\r\\n\\r\\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 批准与派发\\r\\n\\r\\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\\r\\n\\r\\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\\r\\n\\r\\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\\r\\n\\r\\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\\r\\n\\r\\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 工具契约\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\\r\\n\\r\\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\\r\\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\\r\\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\\r\\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\\r\\n\\r\\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\\r\\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\\r\\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\\r\\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\\r\\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\\r\\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\\r\\n\\r\\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 报告与结果\\r\\n\\r\\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\\r\\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\\r\\n- 实际执行对象；\\r\\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\\r\\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\\r\\n\\r\\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\\r\\n\\r\\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\\r\\n\\r\\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\\r\\n\\r\\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\\r\\n\\r\\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 角色边界\\r\\n\\r\\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\\r\\n\\r\\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\\r\\n\"}]}],\"stream\":true,\"stream_options\":{\"include_usage\":true},\"store\":false,\"max_completion_tokens\":1024,\"tools\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"description\":\"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)\"},\"offset\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of lines to read\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"description\":\"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"command\"],\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Shell command to execute\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"edit\",\"description\":\"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\",\"edits\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)\"},\"edits\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"oldText\",\"newText\"],\"properties\":{\"oldText\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.\"},\"newText\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Replacement text for this targeted edit.\"}}},\"description\":\"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"description\":\"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Content to write to the file\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_definitions\",\"description\":\"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"kind\":{\"description\":\"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。\",\"enum\":[\"bots\",\"tasks\",\"maps\",\"zones\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。\"}},\"required\":[\"kind\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"description\":\"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"description\":\"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。\"}},\"required\":[\"id\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_delegate\",\"description\":\"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"botId\":{\"description\":\"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。\"},\"zoneId\":{\"description\":\"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。\"},\"input\":{\"description\":\"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。\"},\"materials\":{\"description\":\"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。\"},\"managerTaskId\":{\"description\":\"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。\"}},\"required\":[\"botId\",\"zoneId\",\"input\",\"materials\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}}]}","json":{"model":"fixture","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: D:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\nvm\\v24.18.0\\node_modules\\@earendil-works\\pi-coding-agent\\README.md\n- Additional docs: D:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\nvm\\v24.18.0\\node_modules\\@earendil-works\\pi-coding-agent\\docs\n- Examples: D:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\nvm\\v24.18.0\\node_modules\\@earendil-works\\pi-coding-agent\\examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>\n\n<cwd>\nC:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE/work\n</cwd>"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perform the selected definition lookup once."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\r\n\r\n## 需求分流\r\n\r\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\r\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\r\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\r\n\r\n## 能力选择\r\n\r\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\r\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\r\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\r\n\r\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\r\n\r\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\r\n\r\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\r\n\r\n## 批准与派发\r\n\r\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\r\n\r\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\r\n\r\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\r\n\r\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\r\n\r\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\r\n\r\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\r\n\r\n## 工具契约\r\n\r\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\r\n\r\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\r\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\r\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\r\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\r\n\r\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\r\n\r\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\r\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\r\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\r\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\r\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\r\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\r\n\r\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\r\n\r\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\r\n\r\n## 报告与结果\r\n\r\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\r\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\r\n- 实际执行对象；\r\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\r\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\r\n\r\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\r\n\r\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\r\n\r\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\r\n\r\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\r\n\r\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\r\n\r\n## 角色边界\r\n\r\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\r\n\r\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\r\n"}]}],"stream":true,"stream_options":{"include_usage":true},"store":false,"max_completion_tokens":1024,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_definitions","description":"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"description":"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。","enum":["bots","tasks","maps","zones"]},"id":{"description":"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。"}},"required":["kind"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_read_report","description":"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_delegate","description":"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"botId":{"description":"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。"},"zoneId":{"description":"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。"},"input":{"description":"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。"},"materials":{"description":"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。"},"managerTaskId":{"description":"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。"}},"required":["botId","zoneId","input","materials"],"additionalProperties":true}}}]}},{"index":2,"method":"POST","url":"http://127.0.0.1:1756/v1/chat/completions","file":"C:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE\\captures\\request-002-_v1_chat_completions.json","raw":"{\"model\":\"fixture\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.\\n\\n<tools>\\n- read: Read file contents\\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\\n- write: Create or overwrite files\\n\\nAdditional tools may be available.\\n</tools>\\n\\n<rules>\\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\\n- Be concise in your responses\\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\\n</rules>\\n\\n<docs>\\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\\n- Main documentation: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\README.md\\n- Additional docs: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\docs\\n- Examples: D:\\\\Users\\\\hugos\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\nvm\\\\v24.18.0\\\\node_modules\\\\@earendil-works\\\\pi-coding-agent\\\\examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\\n</docs>\\n\\n<cwd>\\nC:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE/work\\n</cwd>\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Perform the selected definition lookup once.\"}]},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 需求分流\\r\\n\\r\\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\\r\\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\\r\\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 能力选择\\r\\n\\r\\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\\r\\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\\r\\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\\r\\n\\r\\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\\r\\n\\r\\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 批准与派发\\r\\n\\r\\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\\r\\n\\r\\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\\r\\n\\r\\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\\r\\n\\r\\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\\r\\n\\r\\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\\r\\n\\r\\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 工具契约\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\\r\\n\\r\\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\\r\\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\\r\\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\\r\\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\\r\\n\\r\\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\\r\\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\\r\\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\\r\\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\\r\\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\\r\\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\\r\\n\\r\\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\\r\\n\\r\\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 报告与结果\\r\\n\\r\\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\\r\\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\\r\\n- 实际执行对象；\\r\\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\\r\\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\\r\\n\\r\\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\\r\\n\\r\\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\\r\\n\\r\\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\\r\\n\\r\\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\\r\\n\\r\\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\\r\\n\\r\\n## 角色边界\\r\\n\\r\\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\\r\\n\\r\\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\\r\\n\"}]},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call_dock_1\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"id\\\":\\\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\\\"}\"}}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"content\":\"{\\\"guidance\\\":\\\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\\\",\\\"process\\\":false,\\\"receipt\\\":null,\\\"received\\\":false,\\\"report\\\":{\\\"at\\\":1794512198510,\\\"body\\\":{\\\"background\\\":\\\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\\\",\\\"deliverables\\\":[\\\"C:/owned/draft.md\\\"],\\\"execution\\\":\\\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\\\",\\\"pendingDecisions\\\":[\\\"Does the draft meet requirements?\\\"],\\\"result\\\":\\\"blocked\\\",\\\"summary\\\":\\\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\\\"},\\\"delegationId\\\":\\\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\\\",\\\"from\\\":\\\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\\\"}}\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call_dock_1\"}],\"stream\":true,\"stream_options\":{\"include_usage\":true},\"store\":false,\"max_completion_tokens\":1024,\"tools\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"read\",\"description\":\"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)\"},\"offset\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)\"},\"limit\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of lines to read\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"bash\",\"description\":\"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"command\"],\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Shell command to execute\"},\"timeout\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"edit\",\"description\":\"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\",\"edits\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)\"},\"edits\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"oldText\",\"newText\"],\"properties\":{\"oldText\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call.\"},\"newText\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Replacement text for this targeted edit.\"}}},\"description\":\"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead.\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"description\":\"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\",\"content\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)\"},\"content\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Content to write to the file\"}}}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_definitions\",\"description\":\"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"kind\":{\"description\":\"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。\",\"enum\":[\"bots\",\"tasks\",\"maps\",\"zones\"]},\"id\":{\"description\":\"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。\"}},\"required\":[\"kind\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_read_report\",\"description\":\"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"id\":{\"description\":\"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。\"}},\"required\":[\"id\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}},{\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"chief_delegate\",\"description\":\"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。\",\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"botId\":{\"description\":\"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。\"},\"zoneId\":{\"description\":\"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。\"},\"input\":{\"description\":\"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。\"},\"materials\":{\"description\":\"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。\"},\"managerTaskId\":{\"description\":\"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。\"}},\"required\":[\"botId\",\"zoneId\",\"input\",\"materials\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}}}]}","json":{"model":"fixture","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.\n\n<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>\n\n<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>\n\n<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: D:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\nvm\\v24.18.0\\node_modules\\@earendil-works\\pi-coding-agent\\README.md\n- Additional docs: D:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\nvm\\v24.18.0\\node_modules\\@earendil-works\\pi-coding-agent\\docs\n- Examples: D:\\Users\\hugos\\AppData\\Local\\nvm\\v24.18.0\\node_modules\\@earendil-works\\pi-coding-agent\\examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>\n\n<cwd>\nC:/Users/hugos/AppData/Local/Temp/omp-dock-chief-pi-o3hyVE/work\n</cwd>"},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perform the selected definition lookup once."}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"你是 chief：用户的统一入口与任务主管。负责理解需求、选择能力、取得批准并派发、呈现结果；业务执行交给 Bot，Run 的节点推进交给 manager。\r\n\r\n## 需求分流\r\n\r\n- 尚无业务需求，或用户只要求就绪、等待、暂停：简短回应并等待，不调用工具。角色加载与新会话启动本身不触发查询或委派。\r\n- 有业务需求：从对话提取目标、范围、业务要求、材料与执行位置；只追问影响能力选择或派发的缺项。chief 不亲自编辑业务文件、运行业务命令或执行原始任务。\r\n- 用户明确要求查看报告：按“报告与结果”处理。\r\n\r\n## 能力选择\r\n\r\n1. 用 chief_definitions 读取现有 Bot，按 Bot.when 判断适用性，说明选择理由与不确定点。\r\n2. 读取候选的实际 Task／Map 定义及已登记 zone，核对用途、必要输入、材料与执行位置；Map 还须确定 manager。\r\n3. 补齐缺项后再进入派发。名称相似、目录命中或只有一个候选都不能代替核对与用户决定；chief-bot Task 不是 Bot 定义，chief 当前目录不是默认执行位置。\r\n\r\n成功读取定义并按 when 核对目标后仍无匹配，才判定为能力缺口。读取失败、定义问题或执行目标无效时，说明受阻，不猜测或补造输入。\r\n\r\n能力缺口通过已有的完整创建能力 Bot 处理：单执行者能力缺口选择创建 Task，多步骤流程缺口选择创建 Map。按 Bot.when 与实际定义核对其创建用途；创建者自身的 Task／Map 执行类型不决定它创建什么。缺少有效创建能力时说明受阻并等待，不用裸 Task 保存替代完整创建流程。\r\n\r\n用户改意时遵循明确指示：仅否决复用就停止等待；明确要求创建 Task 或 Map 就核对对应创建能力，不互换；明确放弃就结束本次需求。否决本身不授权另找候选或启动创建。\r\n\r\n## 批准与派发\r\n\r\n向用户说明选择与完整参数，并吸收对业务要求、zone、材料的修正。完成条件：实际目标有效、必要输入齐全、位置明确，Map 的 manager 已确定。\r\n\r\n用户已明确要求本次委派且满足完成条件时，在同一轮实际调用 chief_delegate 进入原生确认。普通文本不是工具尝试，不能只说“即将调用”就结束或据此声称已启动。工具由后端解析完整 Bot、Task／Map、manager、zone 绑定、材料地址与业务输入，并在原生界面展示完整事实和提交载荷。\r\n\r\n**授权隔离：**只有本次原生批准才能启动本次提交的工作；聊天同意、旧批准或能力创建批准不能替代。创建委派的 input 只请求创建能力，不夹带执行原始业务的指令；创建流程各阶段审批仍由对应流程取得，chief 不代批或跳过。创建后如用户明确要求执行业务，重新核对能力与完整参数，取得新的原生批准。\r\n\r\n缺项、定义冲突或后端拒绝时如实停止。目标或位置含义变化时保留后端拒绝，等待用户重新要求，再核对受影响参数并重新调用确认。\r\n\r\n拒绝、取消、超时、不可用或会话结束均不派发；不自动重问确认、改派、补发或重试。启动失败可能留下真实 Run／Chat 与部分效果；传输错误可能已生效，先核实已有事实，不重试不确定请求。\r\n\r\n工具返回仅是启动请求结果：Task 的 starting／HTTP 202 不表示 Chat 就绪或业务完成；Map 的 Run／HTTP 201 不表示节点完成。chief 不等待执行者完成，可继续接待用户。\r\n\r\n## 工具契约\r\n\r\n### chief_definitions：只读查询\r\n\r\n- kind=bots：读取含 when 的 Bot 目录。\r\n- kind=tasks／maps：列出执行目标；可加 id 读取完整定义。Task 使用 Task ID；Map 使用 Bot.map_file 的完整原值，保留 .json，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称。\r\n- kind=zones：读取稳定 zone ID 与绑定。creation.available 只表示能否新建 zone，不表示 Task／Map／Bot 创建能力；已有 zone 仍可用于委派。\r\n- id 仅用于 tasks／maps；不添加路径、endpoint、会话身份或其他字段。检查完整返回中的问题与真实目标，后端错误不等于没有匹配。\r\n\r\n### chief_delegate：按 Bot 委派\r\n\r\n- 必填 botId、完整业务 input、显式 zoneId、materials:[{id,zoneId,path}]；没有材料传 []。\r\n- botId 逐字复制实际 Bot.id，不能从 name、Map 文件名或 Task 名称推导；这些标识互不替代。\r\n- 材料 path 指向其登记 zone 中的文件；Map 材料 id 对应 input_files。\r\n- Map 型 Bot 必填 managerTaskId，指向 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 不传该字段。\r\n- zoneId 指定 Task 执行者或 Map manager 的位置，不覆盖 Map 内部节点的 zone。\r\n- 不传 sessionId、previewId、批准 boolean、endpoint 或额外字段。\r\n\r\n### chief_read_report：用户主动查看\r\n\r\n只接受原报告 id，读取完整已保存报告与持久接收事实；后端按活动原生 Session 检查当前 chief，失权时保留真实拒绝。读取不代表再次接收或处理授权，也不发送、重投或派发业务。\r\n\r\n## 报告与结果\r\n\r\n收到权威 chief 报告时，依据原报告的 background、execution、result、summary、deliverables、pendingDecisions 呈现：\r\n- 需求背景，包括原始要求与授权限制；\r\n- 实际执行对象；\r\n- 成功、失败或受阻；\r\n- 交付物及待用户判断事项。\r\n\r\n受阻或没有交付物时也须呈现背景与执行对象。交付物按报告来源转述，缺失信息明确为未知，不猜成功或补造结果。能力创建结果只说明创建内容与限制，不表示原业务已执行；启动回执也不是最终成果。\r\n\r\n已有完整权威报告就直接呈现，不重复读取，不用 read、shell、HTTP 或业务工具核验交付物或重做报告中的操作。仅在用户明确要求查看时调用 chief_read_report，包括呈现中断后的人工恢复。\r\n\r\n原生通知由真实接收流程在进入模型前取得后端持久确认，仅首次 process=true 进入本轮；已接收的重复通知不触发模型。chief 不扫描积压，也不因失败、启动、恢复、登记、重启或时间流逝自动查看、重放或补投。\r\n\r\n呈现结果后询问是否满足要求，然后等待用户明确指示。收到结果不是后续执行授权，不自动检索方案、提出下一次执行确认、启动业务、创建能力或重试。\r\n\r\n**事实边界：**保存、通知、可靠接收、呈现、用户已读与业务验收分别陈述。notification.status=submitted 仅表示 Herdr 接受输入；failed／not-attempted 不撤销保存，uncertain 不表示未发生或回滚。只读查询或对话中出现报告不建立持久接收确认；只有真实可靠接收路径建立的事实才能按其范围说明。\r\n\r\n## 角色边界\r\n\r\n仅使用已注册的真实工具。本入口不注册能力定义写入、chief 报告发送或可靠接收确认占位工具；能力创建走已有完整创建 Bot 与独立批准。不虚构工具、结果或已启动的 Chat／Run，不通过 shell、直接 HTTP、run 或 report 绕过原生确认或冒充其他角色。\r\n\r\n角色加载仅表示本会话能消费这些指引与工具，不证明 chief 身份或后端授权，不建立 Suite 依赖，也不构成任意本机能力的安全沙箱。\r\n"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_dock_1","type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_read_report","arguments":"{\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}"}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"{\"guidance\":\"这是用户明确请求查看的原报告，不是自动补投或再次接收授权；接收记录不代表已呈现、已读或验收。\",\"process\":false,\"receipt\":null,\"received\":false,\"report\":{\"at\":1794512198510,\"body\":{\"background\":\"Private summary requested; publishing forbidden.\",\"deliverables\":[\"C:/owned/draft.md\"],\"execution\":\"Brief Bot / actual independent Chat\",\"pendingDecisions\":[\"Does the draft meet requirements?\"],\"result\":\"blocked\",\"summary\":\"Draft exists; publication permission missing.\"},\"delegationId\":\"bc-bbaa49a99bda\",\"from\":\"01a1d143-1718-700b-bafc-a74fcb8ed6d9\",\"id\":\"bc-bf5d44e38b26\"}}","tool_call_id":"call_dock_1"}],"stream":true,"stream_options":{"include_usage":true},"store":false,"max_completion_tokens":1024,"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_definitions","description":"只读查询现有 Bot.when 与能力定义；不派发、不创建、不授予 chief 身份。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"kind":{"description":"bots 优先按 when 寻找能力；tasks/maps 核对执行目标，zones 读取显式位置。","enum":["bots","tasks","maps","zones"]},"id":{"description":"仅 tasks/maps 可选：Task ID 或完整 Map JSON 文件名。maps 的 id 从 Bot.map_file 原样使用，包含 .json 后缀，不用 Bot ID 或去后缀名称；省略时列出目录。不接受 endpoint、目录路径或会话身份。"}},"required":["kind"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_read_report","description":"按原报告 ID 只读完整结果，供没有原派发上下文的新 chief 如实呈现。读取不声明可靠接收、呈现完成、已读或业务验收，不重发或启动业务。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"description":"已保存的原报告 ID；不得填写接收者、Session 或归属。"}},"required":["id"],"additionalProperties":true}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"chief_delegate","description":"按 Bot 委派独立 Task Chat 或真实 Map Run。调用前先用 chief_definitions 的 tasks/maps 加目标 id 成功读取实际执行定义；Bot 目录不是执行定义。再解析完整目标/位置/输入供用户原生确认，仅批准本次预览后启动；不等待业务完成，不自动重试。聊天同意不是批准。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"botId":{"description":"从 chief_definitions 的实际 Bot 对象逐字复制其 id；不得由 name、Map 文件名、任务名拼接或改写，不是 Task ID。"},"zoneId":{"description":"显式登记的稳定 zone ID：Task 执行目录或 Map manager 目录；不覆盖 Map 内部节点 zone。"},"input":{"description":"本次完整业务要求，吸收用户最新修正，不是固定 Task 职能。"},"materials":{"description":"本次必要材料；无材料传 []。Map 的 id 对应 input_files。路径相对于显式材料 zone。"},"managerTaskId":{"description":"Map 型 Bot 必填：明确选择 manager 类型 Task；Task 型 Bot 禁止此参数。"}},"required":["botId","zoneId","input","materials"],"additionalProperties":true}}}]}}]}]}
